 Alternatively, replace `IsConnected univ` by `IsPreconnected univ` if empty spaces should count as connected.\n\nSearch route: none. The definitional empty-space countermodel settled the issue before component APIs or literature were relevant. No literature anchor was needed.\n\nFile/statements changed: none. Sorry count: **2 → 2**. Commit SHA: none.\n\nFinal command:\n\n```text\n$ lake env lean problems/t94J01/lean/Main.lean\nproblems/t94J01/lean/Main.lean:36:27: warning: try 'simp' instead of 'simpa'\n\nNote: This linter can be disabled with `set_option linter.unnecessarySimpa false`\nproblems/t94J01/lean/Main.lean:47:8: warning: declaration uses `sorry`\nproblems/t94J01/lean/Main.lean:56:8: warning: declaration uses `sorry`\n```\n\nMemory usage:\n\n- `[dispatch-recall-outcome=completed-with-memories]`\n- Ignored `e-codexpilot-zulip-general-topology-complement-connected-component-anchor`: its recorded scope is unrelated to the empty-space obstruction.\n- Ignored `e-codexpilot-turn-component-membership-into-interior-membership-via-openness`: no component argument is reached.\n- Ignored `e-codexpilot-count-polynomial-lemniscate-components-by-roots-plus-one-exterior`: unrelated domain.\n- Ignored `e-codexpilot-frontier-of-open-connected-component-lies-in-ambient-frontier`: no frontier argument is reached.\n- No compile errors occurred, so error-time recall was not invoked.", :excursion-id "E-memory-topology", :clocked-excursion "E-memory-topology", :clocked-target "E-memory-topology"}, :session-id "4fc6f9c2-1807-40ac-8721-d38eb588cfe9", :tags [:claude :chat :turn :user], :at "2026-07-31T17:47:41.909199862Z", :type :coordination, :subject #:ref{:type :session, :id "4fc6f9c2-1807-40ac-8721-d38eb588cfe9"}, :author "joe", :claim-type :question, :id "emacs-5316380eeecbaf437e8e1b873e35f645"}} {:score -11.37365894257471, :entry #:evidence{:body {:session-uuid "019f9b12-3f1e-7471-a926-94d7c2003a09", :turn-id "019fb494-06d5-7970-9b06-a1502b81549f", :event-seq-range [5224 5237], :reasoning-encrypted-only-count 0, :tool-digest-count 2, :rollout-file "/home/joe/.codex/sessions/2026/07/25/rollout-2026-07-25T21-58-12-019f9b12-3f1e-7471-a926-94d7c2003a09.jsonl", :turn 42, :event :turn-round, :truncated? false, :message-count 4, :harvester-version 1, :reasoning-count 1, :profile :codex-rollout, :text "Codex rollout turn 42\n\nREASONING (plaintext available in rollout)\n**Compiling detailed final summary**\n\nAGENT MESSAGES\nI’m finishing the handoff with a fresh compile and repository-state check; the analytic homotopy package is committed, while the argument-principle bridge remains the precise frontier.\n\nI’m finishing the handoff with a fresh compile and repository-state check; the analytic homotopy package is committed, while the argument-principle bridge remains the precise frontier.\n\nOutcome: blocked at the genuine argument-principle frontier. I committed an axiom-clean analytic homotopy package, without weakening or relocating the remaining theorem.\n\nCommit: `929e7cade198a20269e6010ea65974cee5bd5924`  \nMessage: `rouche: package analytic homotopy frontier`\n\nRoute taken:\n\n- Standard route: the **Argument Principle**, followed by homotopy invariance of the closed one-form `dz/z`.\n- I accepted the suggested identification of the frontier but corrected the implementation plan: current Mathlib has a Poincaré-style homotopy theorem for curve integrals, making that preferable to the previously rejected covering-space lift. It still lacks the argument-principle bridge from the logarithmic derivative integral to the divisor count.\n\nSearch audit:\n\n- Arm (a), components, carried the partial and identified the exact missing bridge.\n  - Loogle `MeromorphicOn.divisor ?f ?s`: found divisor support/restriction APIs, including `divisor_sphere_support_finite`, `divisor_congr_codiscreteWithin`, and `divisor_apply`.\n  - Loogle `AnalyticOnNhd ℂ ?f ?s → _`: found analytic circle-average/Jensen components.\n  - Loogle `circleIntegral (fun z ↦ deriv ?f z / ?f z) ?c ?R`: zero matching declarations.\n  - Loogle `windingNumber` and `Rouche`: no useful declarations.\n  - LeanSearch “argument principle number of zeros of a holomorphic function inside a circle”: returned elementary circle-integral/Cauchy components, but no argument principle.\n  - LeanSearch “homotopy invariance of winding number for a loop avoiding zero”: found `ContinuousMap.Homotopy.curveIntegral_add_curveIntegral_eq_of_diffContOnCl`.\n  - LeanSearch “sum of divisor of analytic function in a closed ball”: found divisor and zero-extraction components, but no circle-integral equality.\n- Arm (b), Zulip, confirmed the historical gap:\n  - `116395-maths/Argument.20principle.json`\n  - `217875-Is-there-code-for-X?/Cauchy's residue theorem.json`\n  - `Cauchy's residue theorem on punctured disk.json`\n  - `winding number.json`\n  These document the missing residue/argument-principle infrastructure. Current Mathlib has since gained curve-integral and meromorphic machinery, but the bridge remains absent.\n- Arm (c), arXiv, was not needed rather than unsuccessful: the mathematical route was already known, and component searches isolated the formalization gap.\n\nChanges:\n\n- Modified only `ConstructionTargets/Rouche.lean`.\n- Added:\n  - `rouche_homotopy_analyticOnNhd`\n  - `rouche_homotopy_analyticOnNhd_and_ne_zero`\n- These package the complete analytic and boundary-nonvanishing hypotheses for every straight-line homotopy slice.\n- Sorry count: **1 → 1**. The remaining sorry is still `zeroCountInClosedBall_add_eq`.\n\nFinal validation:\n\n```text\n$ lake env lean ConstructionTargets/Rouche.lean\nConstructionTargets/Rouche.lean:95:8: warning: declaration uses `sorry`\n```\n\nExit code: `0`.\n\nAxiom checks, verbatim:\n\n```text\n'ConstructionTargets.Rouche.rouche_homotopy_analyticOnNhd' depends on axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\n'ConstructionTargets.Rouche.rouche_homotopy_analyticOnNhd_and_ne_zero' depends on axioms: [propext,\n Classical.choice,\n Quot.sound]\n```\n\nNo `sorryAx` occurs in either new declaration. I claim no completion for the main theorem.\n\nExact remaining obstruction:\n\n```lean\n(hR : 0 < R) →\n(hf : AnalyticOnNhd ℂ f (closedBall c R)) →\n(∀ z ∈ sphere c R, f z ≠ 0) →\n∮ z in C(c, R), logDeriv f z\n  = (2 * π * Complex.I) * zeroCountInClosedBall f c R\n```\n\nwith the integer count coerced to `ℂ`, or an equivalent divisor-count formulation of the Argument Principle. At the component level, proving it requires transporting `extract_zeros_poles`’ codiscrete factorization to a boundary equality of logarithmic derivatives, then evaluating the finite product’s circle integral.\n\nError → fix log:\n\n- `ContinuousMap.Homotopy.curveIntegral_add_curveIntegral_eq_of_diffContOnCl` was initially unknown because JensenFormula does not import the Poincaré curve-integral module. Error recall returned no memories. Source inspection located the declaration and clarified the future import requirement.\n- `AnalyticOnNhd.const_mul` was unavailable. Replaced it with the compiling composition `analyticOnNhd_const.mul hg`.\n- Broad searches for a packaged Rouché/argument-principle theorem returned only components, so I stopped instead of recreating the missing theorem behind an axiom.\n\nMemory usage:\n\n- `e-codexpilot-diagnose-recall-empty-before-declaring-terrain-gap` — used: independently verified current APIs rather than treating previous recall emptiness as evidence of absence.\n- `e-codexpilot-finish-an-outside-root-count-from-an-inside-count-and-no-boundary-roots` — ignored for this construction proof; it concerns downstream algebraic bookkeeping after the analytic inside-count transfer.\n- `e-codexpilot-override-a-documented-proof-route-when-component-evidence-favors-another` — used: current closed-one-form homotopy infrastructure improved the route over covering-space lifting.\n- `e-codexpilot-order-proof-search-by-known-route-components-before-literature` — used: searched component