ble theorem signature**\n\n**Inspecting Zulip argument principle**\n\n**Exploring Jensen formula for Rouché proof**\n**Defining zero count and divisor sum**\n\n**Defining zeroCount function for holomorphic roots**\n**Formalizing Rouché theorem with zeroCount equality**\n\n**Proving norm inequalities and nonzero boundary conditions**\n\n**Compiling codebase**\n\n**Fixing imports for complex notation and divisor**\n\n**Applying norm_real lemma simplification**\n\n**Planning homotopy invariant theorem**\n**Refining zeroCount definition and proofs**\n**Noting Jensen limitation for homotopy invariance**\n\n**Removing debug prints**\n\n**Completing partial commit for final compile**\n\n**Summarizing exact proof files and fixes**\n**Noting missing homotopy invariant implementation**\n\nAGENT MESSAGES\nI’m taking the Rouché construction target from the exact downstream signatures first, then I’ll do the required bounded Zulip search and inventory Mathlib’s argument-principle/zero-count APIs before choosing the proof route.\n\nI’m taking the Rouché construction target from the exact downstream signatures first, then I’ll do the required bounded Zulip search and inventory Mathlib’s argument-principle/zero-count APIs before choosing the proof route.\n\nThe Zulip anchor is `116395-maths/Argument principle.json`: it explicitly records that Mathlib had Cauchy integrals but no residue/argument-principle formulation, with winding-number infrastructure identified as the obstacle. Current Mathlib now has divisors and Jensen’s formula, but no homotopy-invariance theorem for the total divisor on a disk—the exact bridge Rouché needs. I’m checking whether a polynomial-specialized transfer can avoid that bridge while keeping the reusable holomorphic statement intact.\n\nThe Zulip anchor is `116395-maths/Argument principle.json`: it explicitly records that Mathlib had Cauchy integrals but no residue/argument-principle formulation, with winding-number infrastructure identified as the obstacle. Current Mathlib now has divisors and Jensen’s formula, but no homotopy-invariance theorem for the total divisor on a disk—the exact bridge Rouché needs. I’m checking whether a polynomial-specialized transfer can avoid that bridge while keeping the reusable holomorphic statement intact.\n\nThe reusable interface now compiles: an integer-valued total divisor on the closed disk, the strict boundary inequality, and equality for `f` versus `f + g`. I also proved the entire straight-line homotopy is boundary-nonvanishing. The sole remaining `sorry` is the absent homotopy-invariance-of-total-divisor theorem, not any boundary estimate or analyticity plumbing.\n\nThe reusable interface now compiles: an integer-valued total divisor on the closed disk, the strict boundary inequality, and equality for `f` versus `f + g`. I also proved the entire straight-line homotopy is boundary-nonvanishing. The sole remaining `sorry` is the absent homotopy-invariance-of-total-divisor theorem, not any boundary estimate or analyticity plumbing.\n\nCommitted honest partial as `8814807`.\n\nRoute and literature anchor:\n- Used Mathlib’s meromorphic divisor as the root-count representation.\n- Proved boundary nonvanishing for the full straight-line homotopy `f + t • g`.\n- Zulip anchor: `116395-maths/Argument principle.json`. It identifies the missing residue/argument-principle and winding-number infrastructure. No existing Rouché formalization was found.\n\nChanged only `ConstructionTargets/Rouche.lean`:\n\n- Added `zeroCountInClosedBall`.\n- Axiom-clean:\n  - `add_smul_ne_zero_of_norm_le_one`\n  - `dominant_ne_zero_on_sphere`\n  - `rouche_homotopy_ne_zero_on_sphere`\n- Added the exact reusable Rouché transfer statement `zeroCountInClosedBall_add_eq`, retaining one honest `sorry`.\n\nThe target file was initially absent. Final sorry count: 1. Both downstream problem files remain unchanged with their existing sorries.\n\nFinal gate:\n```text\nlake env lean ConstructionTargets/Rouche.lean\nexi