codex
The implementation now compacts both the in-memory authority and the disk snapshot at the same atomic update boundary; this avoids a false fix where disk shrinks but the JVM keeps—and repeatedly serializes—the large records. I’ve also kept malformed/missing timestamps conservatively unexpired.
