codex
The direct allocation is exactly in `FileChannel.write(ByteBuffer/wrap ...)`: Java copies heap buffers through a per-thread cached direct buffer. I’m replacing only the temporary-file writer with `BufferedWriter` over `FileOutputStream`, then syncing its file descriptor; the directory `FileChannel.force` remains because it writes no payload and preserves rename durability. The existing >3 MB round-trip is the required regression, so no new unpinned test is needed.
