/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/zaif-harness/worklist.edn:131:   :statement "Reading map + data inventory for the U11 actand design pass (discovery only, NO src changes). For each of U11's three arms -- (A) futon3c portfolio/policy.clj:49-74, (B) futon3c aif/mission_head.clj:135-176, (C) the S6 cascade-catalog playout record (wm-side, not built; map what the S6 row and its receipts DO record) -- document: what it computes, its inputs/outputs with verbatim file:line pointers, its grain (arm vs mission), and what recorded data can replay it. Then inventory the replay data U11's acceptance names: the 114 calibration sessions, the 56 live decisions, and the mission-grain tick records -- where each lives (paths/record ids), whether tracked or campaign-data (untracked), and one verbatim sample record id per source. Output: runs/U11-reading-map-v1.md, committed in this row's commit."
/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/zaif-harness/worklist.edn:136:   :statement "Build the actand-indexed world-model source for :task-belief (prerequisite named by D8a's finding :d8/task-belief-actand-source-absent): Z1 promised initial gamma/C/actand tables with provenance (M-zaif-harness.md:187-194); gamma and C exist, the actand table was never built. JOINT PASS AGREED with claude-1 (bellback on invoke-1788372741639, 2026-09-02 ~18:20): claude-2 LEADS the design pass, claude-1 contributes wm-side constraints as review input. The design produces ONE grain-indexed statement in DESIGN-c-vector.md section-5 style (Q_actand : grain -> action -> Density over declared observables) so zaif's arm-grain source and the WM's mission-grain Q(o|pi) hole (DESIGN-c-vector.md section 3) are the same object at two indices -- building two incompatible forward models would recreate the two-C mistake one node over. THREE arms in the registry :choices entry: (A) futon3c portfolio/policy.clj:49-74; (B) futon3c aif/mission_head.clj:135-176; (C) the S6 cascade-catalog playout record (wm-side, NOT built -- named so the registry records it). Arms A/B are runnable over recorded data, so per Joe's 2026-09-01 rule the comparison run is designed into the row, not ruled on in advance. Provenance discipline: a predicted outcome with no typed source is a refusal (D8b's seam), never a prior. NOTE: distinct from wm-contract's own :U11 (C_mis build); same-name different boards."
/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/zaif-harness/worklist.edn:137:   :acceptance "Design draft (runs/U11-actand-design-v1.md, IF/HOWEVER/THEN/BECAUSE) reviewed by claude-1; registry :choices entry naming all three arms; the comparison replay over recorded data (114 calibration sessions + 56 live decisions; tick records for mission grain) with DISCRIMINATION as the headline number -- baselines to beat, named: wm U12 status-quo = 1 distinct risk value over 133 actions across 14 channels; zaif = 1 distinct act value (0.0) over 114/114 sessions. A named provenance-bearing query whose result D8b's seam propagates; one live-shaped demonstration of a real nonzero belief term reaching act-value; D9's replay re-run per arm; default off, flip J-gated."}
/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/zaif-harness/worklist.edn:143:   :acceptance "A live-shaped invoke whose dispatch carries a clocked mission produces an arm-choice record with :mission populated and gamma-for reading that mission's cell (not the 1.0 default); missionless ctx still records a typed absence; test pins both; no regex-widening (the prompt-text fallback must not be the fix). SHARPENED mid-flight (claude-1, D8-review checkpoint reply): 'not the default' must be a TYPED DISTINCTION in the record -- :gamma-source :table-cell | :default-no-mission | :default-table-miss (D8b's typed-absence pattern applied to the gamma channel) -- because until it exists every :gamma-used 1.0 in the live corpus is ambiguous between 'uniform prior' and 'cell that reads 1.0', which also contaminates wm-side B1 analyses over the 114 sessions. Supplement belled to codex-7 in flight; if the delivery predates it, the reviewer adds it (small, same pattern)."}
/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/zaif-harness/worklist.edn:192:   :progress "2026-09-02 ~18:15: D8a LANDED (futon2 c8eec02, runs/D8a-task-belief-sources.md) and REVIEWED by claude-2: single-file path-scoped read-only artifact; five candidate sources each probed and rejected on stated semantics (gamma = double-counted precision; prior decisions = self-referential and outcome-free; posting-stats = one observation rewarding two arms; mission registry/C_mis/C-vector = status and preference, not action-conditioned prediction); spot-checked by reviewer: actand has 12 mentions in holes/M-zaif-harness.md and 0 in any src/ or test/ tree in futon2 or futon3c; Z1's promised actand table (M-zaif-harness.md:187-194) was never built; 114-session replay citation accurate. Typed finding ADOPTED: :d8/task-belief-actand-source-absent. Consequence, stated plainly: the charter's hope that D8 makes belief 'genuinely enter act-value' is refuted as stated -- there is nothing to plumb yet. D8b re-scoped to the typed-absence + provenance-gated acceptance seam; the real source is prerequisite work, minted as U11."
/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/zaif-harness/worklist.edn:193:   :statement "Hydrator supplies no task belief (SURPRISES.md entry 8, review-confirmed, minted as a row 2026-09-02 by claude-2): futon3c/src/futon3c/agents/zaif_inputs.clj hydrate-inputs sets :task-belief {} unconditionally (~L192), so zaif_controller/act-value's belief term is 0.0 on all 114 recorded sessions and the burned-in gamma (0.7071 for M-futon-forward-model) multiplies zero. Fix direction is the HYDRATOR (supply the belief), not the controller. Declared-inputs discipline applies: the packet must name which TYPED source populates :task-belief (decision evidence, ledger-derived stats, mission record); if no typed source exists yet, that absence comes back as a finding with a typed-empty default, never an invented value."
/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/zaif-harness/worklist.edn:197:   :evidence "futon2 2bd8e5e (codex-17: D9-tie-order-count.edn + regenerate script). Reviewed 2026-09-02 ~20:15: REGENERATION RE-RUN BY REVIEWER, BYTE-IDENTICAL (determinism proven); kondo 0/0, parens OK, path-scoped, controller sha + corpus sha256 + both populations' reconstruction methods recorded; live-pin is a full post-D8b/D10 record (typed absence, :d10/unclocked, :default-no-mission all visible in one replay). HEADLINE: calibration corpus reproduces entry 9 exactly (83/114 tie-settled, all [:act :yield] ties; 31 score-settled :retrieve) AND the corrected expectation held (unchanged post-D8b, as D8a predicted). NEW FINDING, sharpening SURPRISES entry 9's framing: the 56 PERSISTED live decisions replay 0% tie-settled -- all 56 score-settled :retrieve. The tie-order pathology is a property of the calibration corpus's session distribution (weak retrieve signal), not of recorded live traffic; the standing gap remains that :act is structurally 0.0 everywhere (it can never win), but 'live decisions settled by accident' is now 'calibration sessions settled by accident; live decisions settled by arithmetic in which act cannot compete'. Feeds U9/R7 as evidence and is U11's per-arm comparison BEFORE row (the regenerate script is the harness hook, as designed)."
/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/zaif-harness/worklist.edn:199:   :statement "83/114 live decisions settled by case order, not arithmetic (SURPRISES.md entry 9, review-confirmed): with :act and :yield both structurally 0.0 they tie at the maximum whenever :retrieve and :ask score <= 0, and choose-arm's case order takes :act; only the 31 :retrieve choices were arithmetic. Same family as ZU-2's unreachable :ask. EXPECTATION CORRECTED by D8a (2026-09-02): D8b retains the zero fallback, so the replay will show tie behaviour ~unchanged; this row's value is pinning that count as the standing gap attributable to :d8/task-belief-actand-source-absent (U11), not confirming a fix. If a majority still tie after U11 lands a real source, that is the design finding."
