holes/labs/zaif-harness/worklist.edn:77:   :progress "2026-09-02, the seam checked at Joe's prompt ('the loop should know that has been selected -- worth checking'): IT DOES NOT. (1) The tick has no active-mission focus: selection is re-derived fresh each tick from the weights; the only persistence is the trace record, read solely for non-progress decay (war_machine.clj:1417-1430). (2) A purpose-built, witnessed active-focus register EXISTS -- clock/clocked-on hyperedges [:person :mission/doc], single-active invariant, witness rules dispatch-mission-id and agent-edit-activity, 66 live edges incl. agent:zai-4 clocked on the v0 zaif mission -- and war_machine.clj never reads OR writes it. Fourth recorded-but-never-consulted instance today. (3) Nothing in the machine currently records the S3 selection: the hand step-throughs wrote no trace and no clock edge, by design. The S4 build: at selection the tick mints a witnessed clocked-on edge for the WM identity (witness rule selection-decision, source = the trace record), honoring single-active; at READ the tick loads that edge as its active task focus, and the clocked mission parameterizes G. NOT done by hand here: minting a clock edge without a true witness would invent evidence, the exact move the registry refuses."
holes/labs/zaif-harness/worklist.edn:84:   :statement "The MAP flight with the cascade catalog as its substrate (Joe 2026-09-02, two rulings: the epistemic-action hole -- futon4/holes/mission-lifecycle-wm-alignment.md 3b -- and the catalog design -- 3c). Two halves, built in order: (a) CATALOG READER: a query that assembles a mission's cascade record from the typed events that already exist (PSR/PUR records, flight discharges, trace decision + :shown lists, clocked-on lineage) and finds kin missions by shared patterns/repos/cross-refs -- read-only, facts first, report which carriers are actually populated vs empty (PSRs sparse, :shown unaggregated, APM rich-but-local, phylogeny 2 edges). (b) :survey-mission ACTION TYPE: a candidate action whose G is dominated by information gain over the mission's unanswered MAP questions plus the kin-catalog gap; discharge = MAP answers as typed observations at mission grain. Candidates opaque at the seam (U5); O5 holds (catalog reading proposes, authors write edges); default off, flip J-gated."
holes/labs/zaif-harness/worklist.edn:131:   :statement "Reading map + data inventory for the U11 actand design pass (discovery only, NO src changes). For each of U11's three arms -- (A) futon3c portfolio/policy.clj:49-74, (B) futon3c aif/mission_head.clj:135-176, (C) the S6 cascade-catalog playout record (wm-side, not built; map what the S6 row and its receipts DO record) -- document: what it computes, its inputs/outputs with verbatim file:line pointers, its grain (arm vs mission), and what recorded data can replay it. Then inventory the replay data U11's acceptance names: the 114 calibration sessions, the 56 live decisions, and the mission-grain tick records -- where each lives (paths/record ids), whether tracked or campaign-data (untracked), and one verbatim sample record id per source. Output: runs/U11-reading-map-v1.md, committed in this row's commit."
holes/labs/zaif-harness/worklist.edn:136:   :statement "Build the actand-indexed world-model source for :task-belief (prerequisite named by D8a's finding :d8/task-belief-actand-source-absent): Z1 promised initial gamma/C/actand tables with provenance (M-zaif-harness.md:187-194); gamma and C exist, the actand table was never built. JOINT PASS AGREED with claude-1 (bellback on invoke-1788372741639, 2026-09-02 ~18:20): claude-2 LEADS the design pass, claude-1 contributes wm-side constraints as review input. The design produces ONE grain-indexed statement in DESIGN-c-vector.md section-5 style (Q_actand : grain -> action -> Density over declared observables) so zaif's arm-grain source and the WM's mission-grain Q(o|pi) hole (DESIGN-c-vector.md section 3) are the same object at two indices -- building two incompatible forward models would recreate the two-C mistake one node over. THREE arms in the registry :choices entry: (A) futon3c portfolio/policy.clj:49-74; (B) futon3c aif/mission_head.clj:135-176; (C) the S6 cascade-catalog playout record (wm-side, NOT built -- named so the registry records it). Arms A/B are runnable over recorded data, so per Joe's 2026-09-01 rule the comparison run is designed into the row, not ruled on in advance. Provenance discipline: a predicted outcome with no typed source is a refusal (D8b's seam), never a prior. NOTE: distinct from wm-contract's own :U11 (C_mis build); same-name different boards."
