holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn:180:   :evidence "SHAS, clause by clause, because this row was built over five slices and no single commit carries it. (b1) THE SOLVER: futon2 a75f763 + 2598fbe (owner review fixes) + 0fb8b27 (bisection replaces the Appendix B gradient stepper as the default), src/futon2/aif/policy_precision.clj:95-395 -- converge-beta, the eq. 2.7 fixed point in one unknown. (b2a) THE ln E ARMS MADE RUNNABLE: futon2 4625524 + cf5c7de + f4c8f9e. (b2b) THE TWO DEBTS NAMED BEFORE ANY WIRING: futon2 352c145 (registry, recorded as C23) + 56700e2 (ledger) -- the ln E placement the live path takes, and the fallback for an unsolved tick. (b2c) THE LIVE WIRING: futon2 5a24194, written and reviewed as RUN8 / stage S3 because that is the row that stages it -- policy.clj:76-145 case :variational-beta-gamma with tau = beta exactly, the parser at war_machine.clj:627-641/643-664, tests and clj-kondo gated there, RUN8 :reviewed-by codex 2026-09-01T20:21:44Z. (c1) THE REGISTRY: futon2 a3aad36, recorded as C24 -- :choices :temperature-update :observed becomes :selection-gain-fold-default-variational-flag-gated with a :realised map. THE ACCEPTANCE CLAUSE THAT IS ONLY HALF PAID, said here rather than left to be discovered: 'a run record shows gamma changing tick to tick from G and pi' is satisfied by RUN7/S2's DARK carry (runs/2026-09-01-s2/, 20/20 records, beta 1.0026460727 -> 1.0343423166, gamma 0.997360910 -> 0.966797920, nothing consuming it), NOT by a live run: RUN8 exercised the live path on two pre-flight ticks and deliberately ran no 20-tick S3 stage run (its :reviewer-should-check (6)). A 20-tick gamma series exists; a 20-tick live tau series does not. If the acceptance meant the latter, this row is not done and the missing thing is a stage run, not more code. THE OTHER STANDING GAP: 'updated by a REVIEWED C row' -- C24 is :done-unreviewed, so this clause clears when C24 is signed, and a reader who rejects C24 rejects this row with it. (c3) THE CLOSING READ, 2026-09-01, claude-20 (build-loop work seat). LEDGER ONLY -- the ledger commit carrying this line; no src/, no registry, no run, so no code sha is owed by this slice and none is claimed. THE CLAUSE THAT WAS OUTSTANDING IS PAID: C24 is :status :done, :reviewed-by codex, :review-covers a3aad36, and aif-equations.edn is UNCHANGED SINCE a3aad36 (git diff a3aad36..HEAD on that file is empty), so codex's signature is over the bytes a reader finds today and not over an earlier state -- that is the failure worklist_check's :covers-key rule exists to catch, checked here by hand as well because it is the whole reason this row waited. EVERY CLAUSE RE-READ AT HEAD eb7c1b0 rather than taken from the ledger, one line each. (1) tau = 1/gamma from the beta update: policy.clj:76-145, case :variational-beta-gamma returns :variational-beta unchanged, with g and adaptive-temperature both out of the expression, and THROWS on a missing or non-finite beta rather than reverting to 1/g (policy.clj:136-145); tau = beta IS tau = 1/gamma because gamma = 1/beta. (2) a run record shows gamma changing tick to tick: runs/2026-09-01-s2/wm-trace-s2.edn carries :policy-precision-state 20 times, 20 DISTINCT gammas, 0.9973609104786869 -> 0.9667979197554702, :beta-source :converged-posterior on 20/20. (3) the selection-gain path remains available under FUTON_WM_TAU_MODE: tau-mode-of (war_machine.clj:627-641) maps only 'spread' and 'variational-beta-gamma' and returns :selection-gain-only for everything else including unset, and arena-tau-mode (war_machine.clj:643-664) is that function applied to the env read and nothing else. (4) tests: clojure -X:test :nses [futon2.aif.policy-precision-test futon2.aif.policy-test futon2.aif.trace-test futon2.report.war-machine-test] -- 152 tests / 684 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors, reproducing the reviewer of 3f889b4's count exactly. (5) clj-kondo: 0 errors 0 warnings over policy.clj, policy_precision.clj, war_machine.clj and trace.clj; check-parens (arxana-check-