ier rows recorded, which is the point -- but it means (c3) would not have caught a defect that was already baked into those artifacts before today."}
holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn:210:   :evidence "futon2 holes/labs/wm-contract/C460-enacted-vs-selected.md. Verdicts per run: wm-trace-2026-07-04.edn DIFFERS, wm-trace-2026-07-05.edn DIFFERS, wm-trace-2026-07-03.edn not determinable (selection is an action on a sorry, enactment is a mission; no join key), the other 54 traces not determinable (no actuation recorded), tick-run-record-2026-08-30/31 not determinable (neither half recorded; :selectorSeam is the declared stub 'stub:first-ranked-authorized-mission'). MECHANISM: in 07-04, rank 1 was :advance-mission M-first-flights among 110 ranked actions; the two gated missions (M-canon-fingerprint-store fail, M-bayesian-structure-learning pass) were BOTH present in the ranked-action targets, so gating was not restricted to unranked candidates -- the rank-1 selection simply was not gated, and the first passing lower-ranked candidate was enacted. THIS FALSIFIES H1 AS WRITTEN: H1's falsifier is 'a run in which the enacted action differs from the recorded Q(pi) selection', and 07-04/07-05 are that run. H1 should be revisited by its reviewer -- closed by record as refuted, or restated as a bound on when the paths agree -- rather than left open. NOT amended here: rewriting another row's Lean declaration on the strength of this report is the reviewer's call. LIMITS in the report section 6: the informative records are July 2026 and the code has moved (v0.15, v0.25 flags), so persistence on current code is not established; and no record pairs a full_loop_runner enactment with a decision, so only close-loop!'s path is compared."
