holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn:457:   :evidence "futon2 5a24194. THE PAIR, changed together as the acceptance requires because one throws on a mode the other admits: the parser is tau-mode-of at war_machine.clj:494-508 -- extracted as a PURE fn so a test drives it with strings instead of mutating the environment -- with arena-tau-mode at war_machine.clj:510-528 being that fn applied to the env read and nothing else; the closed dispatch is policy.clj:76-145, tau_eff = beta exactly, with g and tau_spread BOTH out of the expression. NEVER CROSSES LAWS (I1 b2b (2)): carry-beta always yields a finite positive beta (policy_precision.clj:544-560), so a tick that did not both converge and bracket HOLDS upstream and the new :tau-source names which law produced each tick's tau -- policy.clj:56-75 temperature-source, emitted at policy.clj:318,369,519,547 and persisted (strip-decision drops only :softmax-weights and :ranked-actions, trace.clj:168-178). No beta at all THROWS rather than reverting to 1/g (policy.clj:134-142), and the test asserts the throw is not mistakable for the 1/g answer. variational-tau-preconditions! (war_machine.clj:102-130) refuses the mode without FUTON_WM_BETA_DARK / FUTON_WM_FPI_DARK / FUTON_WM_TRACE_POLICY_DETAILS, where every tick would hold beta_0 at tau = 1.0 -- correct, useless, and indistinguishable in a record from a converged carry sitting at 1.0. STRUCTURAL CHANGE, stated because it is the risk: the beta solve is the temperature, so it must precede selection; cascade-policies/cascade-actions/wm-ranked+cascades (war_machine.clj:4903-4931) and the two dark-field bindings (war_machine.clj:4932-4948) moved ahead of controller-decision. Pure let bindings, all inputs bound earlier, nothing between reads them, same join field wm-ranked+cascades so the beta series stays comparable with S2. THE LIVE PATH RAN, TWICE (run8_s3_preflight.clj, env set in the shell so the parser reads the real environment): control tau 1.0 / :tau-source :selection-gain-only / no beta computed; S3 tau 1.0364669814843985 = the solved beta EXACTLY, :tau-source :converged-posterior, gamma 0.9648160702310347, :wm-version :tau-mode :variational-beta-gamma, continuing the S2 carry which closed at 1.034342317. 0 POSTs and 0 .admintoken reads on both, run lock taken and released. Default-path r6_zero_post_preflight PASS in 29.7 s after the reorder. THE MOVEMENT (run8_tau_arms.clj, runs/2026-09-01-s3/ARMS.txt), 3 fields x 20 ticks x 145 candidates, replayed with policy/softmax-weights and policy/effective-temperature THEMSELVES rather than a re-implementation. CONTROL FIRST: at tau_live the replay reproduces each record's own -G/tau scores, :habit-adjusted-ranking order and :softmax-weights-by-candidate-id at delta 0.0 on 60/60 ticks. Only S2 solved a beta series (20 ticks, 1.0026460727 -> 1.0343423166, all :converged-posterior); S1 and S1b persisted no F_pi readback so their beta is NOT recoverable and the arm transplants S2's by tick index -- stated, not hidden, which makes the S1 arm 'the S1 field under the temperatures S2 measured'. RESULT, all three fields: 0 controller rank moves, 0 habit-adjusted rank moves, 0 habit argmax moves, 0 softmax argmax moves; mean softmax TV distance 3.57e-4, mean entropy 4.66727 -> 4.66725 (S1). AND THE ZEROS ARE STRUCTURAL RATHER THAN A NEAR MISS: ordering is by ln E - G/tau, so raising tau adds +G(1/tau_live - 1/tau_s3) to every score, MONOTONE in G, so within one ln E value the order cannot change at all; ln E takes 3 distinct values (spread 3.0445 nats) and the smallest cross-group adjacent margin at tau_s3 is +0.7356, where negative would be a flip. STALE LABELS corrected in the same slice as the row asks: dark_mode_shadow.bb:9-20,128-140,160,170 called the live mode :gamma-only and bound (:decision :selection-gain) to a variable named gamma; the mode has been :selection-gain-only since B-2d and g is the R14 ENGINEERING gain, whose name collides with the variational gamma = 1/beta this row puts on the live path. No computation changed, only what it is called. TESTS: 8 new (policy_test 5, war_machine_test 3) including the parser/dispatch pairing in both directions; 202 tests / 865 assertions over policy, policy-precision, war-machine, trace, habit-prior, operator-flip, run-tick-once, wm-run-lock and efe, 0 failures 0 errors. clj-kondo 0/0 and check-parens exit 0 on every changed file. p4ng negative_controls PASS (16 negative, 10 positive); pointer_check 246 pointers, 0 unresolved. NOT DONE, stated rather than implied: NO 20-tick S3 stage run -- the acceptance asks for movement against the S1 field and a replay measures that exactly and reproducibly, where a fresh run adds a fourth field and not the comparison; runs/2026-09-01-s3/ holds a replay and its README says so. Findings: holes/labs/wm-contract/C469-s3-live-tau.md. This is also I1 slice (b2c), the live wiring, so that slice must not be taken again."
holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn:484:   :progress "(a) DISCOVERY: futon2 b5eebb5, holes/labs/wm-contract/C471-f-scalar-readers.md. The acceptance's own words split this row in two -- \"DISCOVERY FIRST, no removal in the same slice\" -- so :loop-mode was added to make the ledger say what the acceptance already required; it is a description of the row, not a scheduling preference. SLICE (b), THE DISPOSITION, WAS UNTAKEN AT (a) AND IS NOW TAKEN -- see the (b) entry below. Do not take (a) or (b) again. WHAT (b) INHERITS, so it is not re-derived: (1) no consumer in the tick and no :imports of :F, so the row's premise reproduces; (2) the readers are all CHECKERS, and checks/r8_f_contract.clj is a LIVE gate whose era rule fails on the first F-less record because trace.clj:473 stamps :r8/stored-f-controller-v1 unconditionally -- so \"the diagnostic's reader\" is the check that verifies the diagnostic is written, which (b) must name plainly rather than count as a consumer; (3) cost is 1.9e-8 of a tick and 0.0043% of a record, so cost argues neither way; (4) THE BLOCKING FINDING: war_machine.clj:4915 is the only :R8 route tag, so removal contracts the route to R3->R5, which run3_conformance.bb classifies :unmapped -- NOT CONFORMANT. The acceptance's \"a run shows the key absent\" is the same run that breaks RUN3 unless (b) first says what R8 is tagged at afterwards, or the drawn edge changes (Joe's, not this row's). (b) DISPOSITION: futon2 e25b1ae, holes/labs/wm-contract/C472-f-scalar-disposition.md. THE BRANCH IS REMOVE, and that is not my judgement to make or to soften: Joe's J2 ruling forecloses keep-with-reason by name at aif-equations.edn:163-168 -- \"Do not accept it as a diagnostic to keep: retire it\" -- and the one condition he attached (it stays until its replacement is realised and consumed) was discharged by RUN9/S4. The only material (a) produced for keeping does not survive being said plainly: the reader is checks/r8_f_contract.clj, whose job is to verify the