d control-map-edges.edn:120-124's :via/:basis (echoed at edge-census.edn:82) now name a function that no longer exists -- REPORTED NOT REPAIRED, because that row records what WM-RUN2 measured on 2026-08-30 against the receipt it names, which is still true of that receipt. AND THE ONE OPTION 1 DOES NOT FIX: the retagged :R8 goes on standing between the R3 and R5 tags, so C472's R3->R5 gap stays covered -- removing F did not uncover it. NO :decisions ENTRY WRITTEN: under option 1 there is no [:R3 :R5] hop, and C472 s6 step 2 was conditional on option 2. REMOVED: free_energy.clj:184-205, war_machine.clj:4913-4914 (the call), :5241 (judgement key), trace.clj:482 (record key). ERA, NOT A VERSION BUMP: the three conjuncts are now read off a per-era expectation (checks/r8_f_contract.clj:31-46 era-expectations; contract-era :186-201), :r8/retired-f-controller-v1 requires {:f false :gain true :controller true}, trace schema 21, and two new violation classes :era-requires-gain / :era-requires-controller cover the case no earlier era could produce. An unrecognised contract is :malformed, not silently legacy. THE GENERATED LEAN GOT WEAKER ON PURPOSE AND SAYS SO: R8TickLit carries no contract field and the retirement day is MIXED (records earlier on 2026-09-01 carry F), so file date cannot separate the eras at record grain; generatedEraBoundary is now stated over wmTraceR8StoredEra, the pre-retirement records, with the exclusion named in the generated text. The artefact that enforces the contract over every record is :r8EraBoundary :violations. R8-D2-report.lean is on no lakefile (searched). PINNED CENSUS NOT MOVED, against C472 s4: it was already 85 apart from the live corpus, it feeds :recorded-census-delta which is evidence not a check, and no :checks entry reads it. FOUR HISTORICAL-COMPARISON CONTROLS BROKE AND THEIR ANCHORS DID NOT MOVE: three byte-identity controls in trace_test.clj now drop exactly the two retired keys (i5-retired-keys, trace_test.clj:66-84) because re-pinning would replace each claim with \"the last commit changed nothing\", the rot pre-beta-dark-trace-sha was pinned to avoid; and war_machine_test.clj's loader neutralises the retired call in the historical source it compiles -- THE FINDING THERE: \"load a past revision and compare\" couples every past revision to today's library API, and a deletion is what finds that out. THE RUN, stage S5 runs/2026-09-01-s5/: r6 pre-flight PASS (0 POSTs, 0 .admintoken reads), then wm_run.sh 4 14 claude-20 done rc=0 under one RUN12 lock. All four records carry NO :variational-free-energy key -- checked with contains?, not nil? -- with :producer-contract :r8/retired-f-controller-v1, schema 21, :selection-gain present, controller-map shape intact. run3_conformance: CONFORMANT, 0 unmapped, 0 refutations, selection by-run-id, 4 records / 36 hops / 9 distinct, sha 5a66411. ONE RECORD OUTSIDE S5, recorded not tidied: the first launch was killed by a harness timeout mid-tick, the EXIT trap released the lock, and 84ca8231 survives with the same contract and the same absence; run3 selects by :run/id so it is excluded by construction. THREE REDS REPORTED NOT REPAIRED, two of them verified at HEAD with this change stashed: (1) clojure -T:build ci, the repository's own hermetic gate, discovers THREE tests -- the 965 under test/futon2 run only when the directory is named -- so \"CI is green\" has been carrying almost none of this repository's test weight; (2) checks/trace-schema-compatibility FAILs at HEAD too, on a hard-coded 2026-08-31 date range, and the workspace gate invokes only its --negative arm (wm_workspace_gate.clj:433); (3) the in-tick :route-verdict calls six hops unmapped that run3 classifies :route-measured or :excluded-dependency-grain, pre-existing on 2026-09-01 receipts written before this slice -- the same family as C472's run3-vs-gen_live_topology gap."
holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn:489:   :review "Signed, no defect. futon2 6917ba0 (codex-21). Route persisted present-only and UNCONDITIONALLY, justified by measurement rather than assertion: 1,093 bytes for nine hops on a 1,042,451-byte record, 0.105%. 40 tests / 124 assertions, clj-kondo clean, check-parens OK, pre-flight PASS on 6917ba0. Receipt now carries the run id -- confirmed in the pre-flight output, tick-run-record-2026-09-01-5c5d6b26-....edn -- so same-day runs no longer overwrite. THE ROUND-TRIP TEST CHECKS HOP ORDER EXPLICITLY, asserting [:R20 :R12 :R2] rather than presence, which is what RUN3 needs since a route is a SEQUENCE. And the fixture matches the real shape: route-tag (war_machine.clj:4340-4345) emits {:node :via :at}, so a hop is a CONSECUTIVE PAIR and the receipt :fromNode/:toNode form is a derived rendering. Worth stating because RUN3 must pair consecutive nodes, not look for from/to keys. ONE NOTE, not a defect: the I3 golden test still passes because its fixture carries no route, while a real default record HAS legitimately changed by 1,093 bytes. The golden was not regenerated, which is right; its claim is simply narrower than its name suggests. WHAT THE REVIEW DID NOT COVER, and I opened rows for both: the trace record still carries no run id although the receipt now does (RUN11), and nothing prevents two agents starting ticks at once (RUN12) -- which happened while this review was in progress."
holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn:595:   :statement "Trace records carry no run id. RUN10 gave the diagnostic RECEIPT one -- tick-run-record-<date>-<run-id>.edn, so same-day runs stop overwriting -- and left the TRACE on one file per date with nothing in a record to say which run wrote it. On 2026-09-01 two runs went into one file: 20 routeless records from the first S1, then 9 from an aborted re-run, then S1b. The only discriminator is the timestamp, and RUN3 has to select by range instead of by identity."
holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn:756:   :reviewer-should-check "(1) WHERE THE HASH IS TAKEN. I moved the file read inside mission_c/read-criteria from slurp to readAllBytes-then-decode so one read serves both the digest and the parse. That is a change to the READER, not just to the record, and it is the substantive judgement in this row. If you think the digest belongs at the war_machine seam (hash the path next to :criteria-source, leaving read-criteria alone), say so -- it is a smaller diff and it reintroduces a TOCTOU window between the hash and the read, which is the thing U12 asked to close. (2) THE ENCODING CLAIM at mission_c.clj:281-283. I assert (String. bytes \"UTF-8\") reproduces what slurp decoded, on the basis that clojure.java.io's default encoding is the literal \"UTF-8\" and not the platform charset. If that is wrong, a non-UTF-8 criteria file now parses differently than before, which would be a silent behaviour change in a row that claims none. Verify it rather than take it. (3) THE TWO PINNED CONSTANTS in war_machine_test.clj:1633's u12-recorded-source-sha256. They are content hashes of two files that are live in this repo -- holes/missions/M-wm-aif-policy-grain-compliance.md is an ordinary mission doc anyone may edit -- so this test WILL break the day someone edits it, by design. Decide whether that tripwire is wanted in the suite or belongs in a replay script under runs/; if the former, check the docstring says clearly enough that the repair is re-measure-and-update-both, not update-the-pin. (4) PRESENT-ONLY VS ALWAYS-PRESENT. The acceptance says the readback map CARRIES :criteria-source-sha256; I made it present-only, so a readback with :criteria-reason :source-not-found has :criteria-source (a path) and no digest. A reviewer who reads the acceptance as always-present should say so -- the alternative is an explicit typed value (:no-bytes-read) rather than nil, and I did not want to invent a second vocabulary for something :criteria-reason already says. (5) THAT NOTHING LEAKED: git show --stat 4a987ec touches four files, no registry .edn, no p4ng file, nothing under data/. Note scripts/wm_status_report.py and test/wm_status_report_test.py were ALREADY modified in the working tree when I arrived and are NOT mine -- I staged explicit paths, not -a. Three untracked tick-run-record-2026-09-02-*.edn files in the ledger directory are likewise not mine and are why worklist_check still warns about uncommitted content."}
holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn:784:   :reviewer-should-check "(1) THE ASYMMETRY IS THE JUDGEMENT IN THIS ROW. I shifted :range and left :bernoulli alone, on the argument that the Bernoulli term is an exact KL with no missing constant while the range term is a cross-entropy whose constant was never fixed. The uniform alternative -- subtract each kind's own minimum, so a fully satisfied criterion of ANY shape scores exactly 0 -- is arguably more coherent as a composition and would make U12 clause (c)'s satisfied-zero reachable at last. I did not take it because it moves the 4.539889921682063E-5 that runs/U12-c-mis-falsifier/measurements.edn and runs/U16-outcome-semantics/measurements.edn both record, and because that floor is a genuine property of a soft Bernoulli target rather than an artefact. If you read the acceptance's 'provably >= 0 on every spec shape' as asking for the uniform form, say so -- it is a small change to point-mass-divergence-shift and a large change to what the two artifacts mean. (2) THE THIRD LIMB'S WORDING. 'No satisfied criterion scores below an unsatisfied one on the same channel' is ambiguous in sign, because risk_mis is a cost and 'below' could be lower-cost (which is what you WANT of a satisfied criterion) or worse-merit. I tested both readings rather than pick one; check that the ordering test is the one you meant, and that testing both is not hiding a third reading. (3) LOSING ln Z FROM THE RANGE TERM IS A REAL CONSEQUENCE, not just a constant. Before the shift a NARROW band carried a large negative ln Z, so a narrow criterion was cheaper everywhere than a wide one at the same gap; after it, band width enters only through the gap. That is a change in how two range criteria compare to each other, not only in whether one dips below zero, and no test pins the old cross-criterion ordering because nothing consumed it. (4) I CHANGED risk-mis's :risk RATHER THAN ADDING AN ARM, unlike U16. The argument is that U17 asks for a fix ('route range criteria through a proper KL >= 0'), not a comparison, and that risk_mis is read by nothing on a default tick -- FUTON_WM_MISSION_C is off and mission-c-fields binds after selection is final. If you think this needed the U16 treatment (a selector, default unchanged), that is a structural objection to the whole commit and worth making now. (5) THE WEIGHT GUARD IS SCOPE I ADDED. c-mis now throws on a declared weight that is negative, NaN or infinite. It was not in the acceptance; I added it because 'provably >= 0' is false without it. It can reject a caller that previously worked, though no caller in the tree declares weights at all (grep for :criterion-weights: mission_c.clj and mission_c_test.clj only). (6) THAT NOTHING LEAKED: git show --stat f257ff8 touches six files -- two src, three test, aif-equations.edn -- no p4ng file, no generator, nothing under data/ or runs/. holes/labs/wm-contract/workflow-report.edn and the three untracked tick-run-record-2026-09-02-*.edn files were already in the working tree when I arrived and are NOT mine; I staged explicit paths, not -a."}
holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn:793:   :reviewer-should-check "(1) THE DEFAULT MOVED, WHICH IS THE BIGGEST THING HERE. risk-mis with :outcome-semantics omitted no longer returns the raw pref/log-preference number; it returns the ruled arm's, which on the U12 corpus is a typed ABSENCE where a number used to be. That is what J6 chose, but it means every future replay of U12's script differs from its committed artifact in the two places named in :evidence, and I did NOT re-run either artifact. Decide whether U12's runs/ directory should be re-measured under the ruling as its own row, or left as the record of what the machine did before it. (2) THE EXPLICIT-NIL ESCAPE. I kept the pre-ruling path reachable by passing :outcome-semantics nil explicitly, relying on Clojure's :or defaulting only on an ABSENT key. It is exactly the semantics I want and it is pinned by a test, but it is a subtle distinction to leave load on: a caller who writes :outcome-semantics (get opts :arm) and gets nil silently takes the defective path. The alternative is a named fourth value (:pre-J6-raw) and no reliance on nil, which is louder and adds a vocabulary member. Say if you want that. (3) THE MIRROR CONTROL IN U16'S SCRIPT NOW PRINTS 'CONTROL: FAILS -- do not read section 4'. It fails correctly -- it compares the script's mirror against the shipped readback and the shipped readback took the ruling -- but a future re-runner sees a red control on a green change. I left the script untouched because editing an artifact producer would stale the artifact it produced; the other repair is to teach the mirror the ruled arm and regenerate, which rewrites a measurement record. Neither is obviously right and it is not my call. (4) THE GAUGE TABLE LISTS SIX KEYS FOR THREE CRITERIA, one per id vocabulary, on the claim that futon2 161ac09 ported the ingest's three criteria into the doc verbatim and in order. I verified the order by reading both files; nothing enforces it, so if someone reorders the doc's numbered list the doc ids silently bind to the wrong criteria. The alternative is to bind only the ingest's named ids and let the doc route stay unmeasurable, which is safer and gives up the acceptance's 3/3 on the doc. (5) THE GAUGE OBSERVABLES ARE PRODUCED BY NOTHING. :worklist-acceptance-state, :reporting-gate-test-result and :registry-gap-list-present are not R2 channels and no code emits them, so on a live tick the three criteria read :undeclared-observable -- a missing producer rather than prose. That is honest and it is also the whole remaining distance to a measurable mission; the 3/3 in the acceptance is with the values supplied by a test. Check that you read the acceptance the same way I did. (6) SCOPE I ADDED BEYOND THE ROW: :refused-outcomes and :outcome-semantics on the readback record (argued in :evidence), the :non-binary-value-on-binary-observable reason under arm 2, and validation throws on a malformed :observable-kind or :threshold at construction. Each is small and each is a decision. (7) A POINTER I MOVED AND DID NOT RE-ANCHOR. Inserting the declaration block above c-distribution pushed pref/log-preference's Bernoulli branch from preferences.clj:242 to :292, and :measured and :flip-is-j-gated in the same registry entry still say :242-244 -- text U13 and U17 signed. I recorded the drift in the new key and left the signed prose alone rather than re-anchoring it inside a row whose registry edit is supposed to be additive; pointer_check does not catch this class because it resolves line RANGES and not content, which is the same hole U10 found in C5's pointers. If you would rather the two were re-anchored under the supersession this row already takes, say so. (8) THAT NOTHING LEAKED: git show --stat 5af75e6 touches six files -- three src/scripts, three test -- and this commit touches aif-equations.edn and worklist.edn. No p4ng file, no generator, nothing under data/ or runs/. The three untracked tick-run-record-2026-09-02-*.edn files were in the working tree when I arrived and are not mine; I staged explicit paths, not -a."}
