151-The design, thought through against what exists:
152-
153-1. **The record accretes; nobody writes it after the fact.** A mission's
154-   cascade record is assembled from typed events that already exist or are
155-   already required: PSR/PUR records (the lifecycle mandates per-mission
156-   Pattern Selection Records — which pattern, where, how), flight discharges
157-   (㉚, typed implementation/discharge events), the trace's decision + :shown
158-   pattern lists per tick, and clocked-on lineage (who was on it, when). The
159-   DOCUMENT phase — R17 in the §2 table — is where the accreted record is
160-   sealed as the mission's deposit. The alignment earns its keep here: DOCUMENT
161-   was already "the learning deposit"; this says concretely WHAT is deposited.
162:2. **MAP reads the catalog, not the prose.** The survey flight (S6) queries
163-   kin missions (kinship: shared patterns, shared repos, cross-refs) for their
164-   cascade records — which patterns, in what order, with what outcomes. The
165-   ChipWits reading: you learn to wire a new robot by opening saved robots
166-   from the Warehouse, not by reading their marketing copy.
167-3. **This is where Q(o|π) at mission grain comes from.** P-validated-R5
168-   demands Q(o|π) be DERIVED (a playout), never authored. For a mission-grain
169:   policy there is no simulator — but the catalog IS the playout record:
170-   the empirical distribution of how cascades-like-this-one actually went.
171-   G over candidate build strategies gets its forward model from precedent,
172-   which is also exactly what makes ambiguity discriminate at mission grain
173-   (a strategy with no precedent is high-ambiguity; surveying reduces it).
174-4. **The precedent is already running.** Every APM frame leaves an end-to-end
175-   record (ledger, trace, memories); the zai-scribe mines failed and
176-   successful attempts into typed memories; the fingerprint audit adjudicates
177:   what transferred by token witness. The mission cascade catalog is that
178-   architecture at mission grain, and it should inherit the discipline whole:
179-   typed use records, witnessed transfer, author≠reviewer on anything
180-   promoted from a record into the library.
181-5. **O5 holds.** Catalog reading yields proposals and weights; only authors
182:   write edges. A build strategy learned from the catalog reaches the library
183-   as a proposed pattern with provenance, not as an inferred edge.
184-
