holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn:109:   :review "Read 846fa93. ACCEPTED UNDER THE CURRENT REGISTRY, AND THE REGISTRY IS PROBABLY WRONG HERE: aif-equations.edn :precision at R7 imports [:o :eps0], which is what forces R2->R7; but precision.clj:116-135 computes production precision as the bounded variance component of the ERROR (new-error), with observed entering only the separately-emitted :salience term (default :salience-mode :separate). So at symbol grain R7 imports eps (R8->R7), and R2->R7 is a route-grain fact the file already carries twice, as the agent said. The right fix is to the registry (opened C10, mine, gated for a second read); when C10 lands, this :decisions entry should be retired by a decision citing C10 -- opened D10. Not rejected now because the figure must match the registry it is derived from, and today the registry says o." :owner :wm-organization
holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn:111:   :evidence "p4ng 846fa93. :decisions :r2-r7-o-realised-undrawn (:grounds :code) adds [[:R2 :R7]] :label \"o\". Pointer verified: observation read per channel into fe/compute-prediction-error at war_machine.clj:4375-4379, and precision/update-precision-state called with prec-state and those raw-errors at :4382-4384. REVIEWER, and this row is the weakest of the six -- rejecting it costs the registry nothing: (1) GRAIN -- update-precision-state receives raw-errors, NOT observation, so at symbol grain R7 imports the errors; this same file already records the finer path, :route-measured-drawn R2->R3a stating that 'no direct R2-to-R7 call exists'. The edge holds at ROUTE grain, the distinction D6 exists to record. (2) REDUNDANCY -- unlike D5a-D5e, which added pairs absent from the registry, [:R2 :R7] is ALREADY in both :derived-undrawn and :route-measured-drawn, so the figure now draws this pair three times (derived, measured, added). Recorded because the acceptance is explicit and the edge is real at route grain, but :decisions may be the wrong home for a fact carried twice already. negative_controls PASS (12 negative, 7 positive); pointer_check 117 pointers in 3 files, 0 unresolved. Not regenerated (gate, TN 9a)."
