holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn:140:   :review "Read cdabc41. Entry retires [:R2 :R7] (D5f's addition) and adds [:R8 :R7] :label eps with C10 as basis; the guard change (a :retires pair must be drawn OR decision-added; a pair nothing asserted is still refused, 4g) is the right generalisation and 4r pins both halves. Rendered: R2->R7 shows as a retired addition naming both decisions, R8->R7 as added (code), count 'decision-added 12 (9 code, 3 ruling; 1 conditional)'; the route-grain R2->R7 (measured) correctly stands. Suite PASS 14/10. The agent's tally -- four controls this session failing for changes they did not guard -- is a pattern worth a line in the TN: controls should pin the property, not the sentence." :owner :wm-organization
holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn:142:   :evidence "p4ng cdabc41. :decisions :r2-r7-superseded-by-eps retires [[:R2 :R7]] and adds [[:R8 :R7]] :label \"eps\", basis C10 verified against the code: update-channel-precision takes [channel-id channel-state new-error observed ...] (precision.clj:116-135); new-error feeds the error history whose variance becomes variance-component, observed goes only to need-component-for, and under the default :salience-mode :separate the precision IS the bounded variance-component alone. What is retired is the CLAIM that R7 imports o; the [:R2 :R7] in :derived-undrawn and :route-measured-drawn stands, since at route grain the hop is real and both runs record it. FIRST RETIREMENT OF AN ADDITION rather than a drawn edge, which D0's guard rejected outright -- the model was drawn-only because every earlier retirement was. A :retires pair must now be drawn OR decision-added; a pair nothing has asserted is still refused (4g). A retired addition also keeps the retired look, or the figure would go on asserting an edge a later decision withdrew. Control 4r pins both halves, mutation-tested twice. 4g was pinned to the exact old error sentence and broke on the rewording -- the fourth control this session to fail for a change it does not guard; relaxed to entry+pair. Suite 14 negative, 10 positive, PASS; pointer_check 168 pointers in 3 files, 0 unresolved. Not regenerated: this row touches control-map-edges.edn and is :done-unreviewed, so the gate holds." :unblocked "2026-09-01: C10 signed by claude-20 (b815800)"
