holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn:155:   :evidence "mathlib4 8601489f95 (branch darktower). Holes.lean:6599 declares dirichletAccumulationImportAbsent as kind HOLE, owner wm-organization, falsifier 'a code path from the tick model's o or mu into R17's concentrations'; registered in mkHole at :6810 with :evidence DirichletConcentrations. The claim held open is an ABSENCE, so finding such a path falsifies it and would close R2->R17 and R1->R17. All four pointers verified: a4a_substrate.clj:46-60 reads hyperedges-by-type :capability/* into a4a/corpus->concentration; actuator_a3.clj:31 and :68 write those :capability/* hyperedges, discharge records at :486-487; a4a.clj:2-6 states the namespace is pure and its concepts demo-validated 'until real :capability/* production writes flow'. So the two edges are not a missing wire between agreeing boxes but two accumulations over different data -- a different repair. PROCESS NOTE: `find . -name actuator_a3.clj | head -1` returns futon2/scripts/actuator_a3.clj, a 19-line CLI shim, against which lines 31/68/486-487 are past the end and read as stale pointers. There are three copies; the real one is src/futon2/aif/actuator_a3.clj at 891 lines, which is what pointer_check resolves (roots include src/futon2/aif/ but not scripts/). The pointers are correct; head -1 over a multi-file find manufactures absences. lake build DarkTower.WarMachine.Holes: completed successfully, 2704 jobs, exit 0; hole count 7 -> 8. REVIEWER: Lean edits are reviewed by wm-nouns."
