holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn:193:    :slice-e-d-row "DONE 2026-09-01 (claude-20, wm-edge-loop CLI seat). p4ng 085f758. The D row RUN9 left owed: control-map-edges.edn :decisions gains :r4-r8-q-o-pi-into-f-pi (:adds [[:R4 :R8]], :label \"Q(o|pi)\") and :r8-r6-f-pi-into-posterior (:adds [[:R8 :R6]], :label \"F_pi\"), both :grounds :code. BOTH CARRY :condition, so they render in the conditional class D9 added rather than as unconditional dependencies -- the flags are default off, and R8->R6 has a second condition beyond the flag: complete-or-off coverage. That is not decorative. I read the four S4 trace records myself rather than taking RUN9's summary: :decision :f-pi-posterior is :present :applied? true on dd00675b (F_pi -13.297..-12.543), 200b894f and 5bd37efe (-19.716..-18.962), and :absent :incomplete-coverage with :uncovered-count 1 on 73282cf8 -- so the term is in a run record, and the edge is absent on a quarter of the ticks of the only run that has exercised it. POINTERS VERIFIED HOP BY HOP, not end to end: for R4->R8, efe.clj:602 (fm/predict) -> efe.clj:832 (:prediction on the compute-efe output) -> efe.clj:917 (mapped over every candidate) -> trace.clj:138-149 (:prediction-mean, :prediction-variance, :prediction-variance-status persisted under *persist-policy-trace-details?*) -> war_machine.clj:296-306 (f-pi-dark-readback hands those three keys to f-pi-vector) -> policy_free_energy.clj:100-144. For R8->R6, war_machine.clj:5095-5096 (join against wm-admissible) -> :5105 (:f-pi-opts) -> policy.clj:490-531 -> policy.clj:418-421 -> policy.clj:172-201 (F_pi subtracted, unscaled). TWO THINGS THE FIGURE CANNOT SAY, both in the entries' :notes rather than left implicit. (1) R4->R8 IS DRAWN WITHIN A TICK AND PERFORMED ACROSS ONE: the Q(o|pi) crossing it is the PREVIOUS tick's prediction, joined to this tick's candidates by action identity. The registry's other across-tick carry, :belief-state importing :mu-next, is drawn the same way as R3->R1, so the figure has no vocabulary for the distinction -- D0b's shape, one more time. (2) :policy-free-energy also imports :o, and that pair [:R2 :R8] is ALREADY decision-added by :r2-r8-o-realised-undrawn on the eps basis, so one drawn edge now stands for two distinct symbol-grain imports and its label names only one of them. I DID NOT REVIVE R8->R5: D1 recorded it as carrying no data, and R5 reads neither F nor F_pi. Rendered to stdout only to check the classes -- decision-added 14 (11 code, 3 ruling; 3 conditional), both new edges in the conditional group with their conditions in the title -- and NOT regenerated into a publish (gate, TN 9a). The committed aif-conformance.edn already carries [:R4 :R8] and [:R8 :R6] in :realised-undrawn, so the amber layer and the decision layer will now both draw them, exactly as they already do for R2->R8, R8->R3 and R8->R7."
holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn:205:   :reviewer-should-check "Four things, in order. (1) THE NEW HELPER mkRefutedByRecord is the one piece the acceptance does not name; it said 'mkWitnessedClosed or the registry's refuted form'. I read 'the registry's refuted form' as licence to add one, because mkWitnessedClosed would emit :decided 2026-08-31 for a 2026-09-01 refutation. If a reviewer would rather carry the wrong date than a new helper, it is a three-line revert. (2) THE FIXTURE IS EXTENSIONAL AND UNPINNED. wmTraceR2 and wmTraceR8 beside it carry a content watermark (wmTraceR2ContentPin) so drift in the source corpus is detectable; my two lists carry none, because the trace files are large and no sha convention covers data/wm-trace/. A reviewer may hold that a transcribed census without a pin is a snapshot nobody can re-check -- the counts are re-derivable in seconds with edn/read and the docstrings name files and counts, but the objection stands and the fix is a pin. (3) IS THE RESTATED BOUND WORTH DECLARING AT ALL, given that its antecedent occurs in none of the 50 records? I declared it because the acceptance asked for it by name and the antecedent is producible by a future run; a reviewer may hold that the honest state is one refutation and no successor until a run produces a gated rank-1 selection. (4) lean_sorry_category_check still fails 4 :attestation-checker-absent, unchanged in count. I wrote no checks/*.clj for the new hole: that is an artifact the acceptance does not ask for, and the whole H family shares the gap, so fixing it is one row rather than four."}
holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn:260:   :review "Read d240f8d. This is the row I was asked to doubt, and it stands. Walked every path by which observed could reach production precision: update-channel-precision (precision.clj:116-158) under :separate sets :precision to the bounded variance-component alone, computed by regularized-error-variance (:73-85) over the ERROR history; observed reaches only need-component-for (:110-114) and is emitted as :need-component/:salience. prior-variance (1.0) and prior-strength (1.0) are constants at :45-46, not observation-derived, and the live caller passes neither. The check claude-1 did NOT name is the decisive one: the live caller does not take the default -- war_machine.clj:4382-4385 passes {:salience-mode (arena-salience-mode)}, and arena-salience-mode (war_machine.clj:230-236) returns :separate UNCONDITIONALLY with no env hatch, its docstring saying summed \"is not a live arena configuration because it changes the meaning of Pi\". Also: weighted-error (precision.clj:212-230) reads :precision via precision-for, not :salience, and :salience has no reader anywhere in src/ or scripts/. So no, observed does not reach production precision by any path, D5f's R2->R7 edge should not stand at symbol grain, and the row's \"R2->R7 holds only at route grain\" is the right qualification -- o does enter update-precision-state, it just never reaches Pi." :owner :claude-1
