/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/zaif-harness/worklist.edn:74:   :read-half "2026-09-02 LANDED and REVIEWED: 6b53fd9, path-scoped commit (no collision this time). Gates reproduced in isolated worktree: kondo 0/0, parens OK (with --), 114 tests / 728 assertions across trace + war-machine + readiness namespaces. Focus loaded at READ, attached as a terminal projection after decision -- a good deviation, it makes non-consumption directly testable; rank-identity pinned flag-on vs flag-off. Retraction finding confirmed in the diff: the type query is db-as-of-now (retracted edges server-excluded per clock-lineage docs); a dedicated request distinguishes :no-active-clock from :clock-unreadable because the shared helper collapses errors to []. Defensive latest-clocked-at-ms tiebreak documented. Both S4 halves now built and reviewed, both default OFF. Remaining S4 substance: the clocked mission parameterizing G (C-vector ingest) -- design pass before any packet."
/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/zaif-harness/worklist.edn:77:   :progress "2026-09-02, the seam checked at Joe's prompt ('the loop should know that has been selected -- worth checking'): IT DOES NOT. (1) The tick has no active-mission focus: selection is re-derived fresh each tick from the weights; the only persistence is the trace record, read solely for non-progress decay (war_machine.clj:1417-1430). (2) A purpose-built, witnessed active-focus register EXISTS -- clock/clocked-on hyperedges [:person :mission/doc], single-active invariant, witness rules dispatch-mission-id and agent-edit-activity, 66 live edges incl. agent:zai-4 clocked on the v0 zaif mission -- and war_machine.clj never reads OR writes it. Fourth recorded-but-never-consulted instance today. (3) Nothing in the machine currently records the S3 selection: the hand step-throughs wrote no trace and no clock edge, by design. The S4 build: at selection the tick mints a witnessed clocked-on edge for the WM identity (witness rule selection-decision, source = the trace record), honoring single-active; at READ the tick loads that edge as its active task focus, and the clocked mission parameterizes G. NOT done by hand here: minting a clock edge without a true witness would invent evidence, the exact move the registry refuses."
/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/zaif-harness/worklist.edn:84:   :statement "The MAP flight with the cascade catalog as its substrate (Joe 2026-09-02, two rulings: the epistemic-action hole -- futon4/holes/mission-lifecycle-wm-alignment.md 3b -- and the catalog design -- 3c). Two halves, built in order: (a) CATALOG READER: a query that assembles a mission's cascade record from the typed events that already exist (PSR/PUR records, flight discharges, trace decision + :shown lists, clocked-on lineage) and finds kin missions by shared patterns/repos/cross-refs -- read-only, facts first, report which carriers are actually populated vs empty (PSRs sparse, :shown unaggregated, APM rich-but-local, phylogeny 2 edges). (b) :survey-mission ACTION TYPE: a candidate action whose G is dominated by information gain over the mission's unanswered MAP questions plus the kin-catalog gap; discharge = MAP answers as typed observations at mission grain. Candidates opaque at the seam (U5); O5 holds (catalog reading proposes, authors write edges); default off, flip J-gated."
/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/zaif-harness/worklist.edn:88:   :statement "Live node-trace corpus from the mission the machine actually wants (Joe 2026-09-02: 'turn that mission into a set of live test data for all the nodes that it is going to flow through, and trace it through... maybe we should work with the expressions-of-interest mission, which is the one the machine wanted to select'). WHY M-EOI AND NOT ZAIF AS THE DATA SOURCE: zaif v0 declares no observation model, so U6 had to PLANT R4/R8 and its own negative control proved the orderings belong to the plant; the WM's field IS a real observation model at mission grain, and for M-expressions-of-interest (futon5a/holes/missions/, centrality 0.685, the baseline selector's own choice) every tick generates real per-node data with no plant. Probe already run (2026-09-02, three tick records on disk): R2 = 14 live observation channels; R1/R3 = 417-entry mu-pre/mu-post; R5/R6 = full controller-ranking with per-term decision-explanation, M-eoi rank 1 on run 3; R14 = tau with source; S4 focus read present. Build the extractor: per-node fixture files harvested from live tick records (never planted), keyed by (run-id, node), with a README mapping fixture -> R node -> record field -> pointer. Named gaps to carry, not fill: :precision has no top-level key on the record (locate R7 or record its absence as typed); R16 enactment data does not exist until a flight flies; R17 unchanged. Bonus stated plainly: working WITH the machine's preference removes the compliance fight from the data-collection path entirely, and real flights on M-eoi would produce the grounded changes that stop the non-progress decay from firing (surprise ledger entry 2)."
/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/zaif-harness/worklist.edn:96:   :evidence "futon2 4a44a3a (codex-7, U8b gate + tests) + 5286634 (claude-2 review fixes). Gate: holes/labs/zaif-harness/report_gate.clj; test: report_gate_test.clj (bb, live store, 5 tests / 14 assertions green). Reviewed 2026-09-02: diff read; gates reproduced in isolated sibling worktree futon2-review-claude2 (kondo 0/0, check-parens OK with --, delivered suite 3 tests / 11 assertions ALL GREEN as authored; the 5/14 final count is delivered suite + 2 reviewer-added pinning tests, not a repair of red tests); commit path-scoped, read-only store access, both probe gotchas handled, no zaif-runtime or predicate changes. Two review findings, fixed by reviewer with pinning tests: (1) status 'declared?' was some over :derived-from, so an older commit-subject signal would launder a chat-derived status -- now only the deriving (first) signal vouches; (2) mission recorded-but-different was typed attribution-absent -- now :u8/claim-unbacked, absence reserved for nil record/clock. Acceptance met per adopted verdict: fixture decision passes; planted unbacked claim fails named; real decision fails carrying exactly the two U8a findings, re-derived from the store. POST-D11 ADDENDUM (970001c): the store's overbroad condition is repaired, so the live gate now reports attribution-absent alone; the status absence (nil, 0 signals) backs an absence claim, and the overbroad path stays pinned by fixture. Known data-dependence, stated not fixed: the real-decision test picks a live :zaif-arm-choice from text-search, so it will need updating when D10 lands and new decisions carry :mission (that flip is the D10 acceptance demonstration)."
