/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/zaif-harness/worklist.edn:128:   :evidence "futon3c b13075bf (codex-22) + 9d17fb92 (claude-2 live-pin). Reviewed 2026-09-02: diff read (test-only, path-scoped); gates reproduced at the delivered sha in an isolated sibling worktree (20/76 green with FUTON3C_ZAIF_GAMMA_EDN set -- the D8-row cwd-heuristic micro-finding applies to any sibling worktree); kondo 0/0, parens OK. The pin: planted :prior-turn/:plan/:horizon leave decide and dual-decide byte-identical; exact output-key allowlists on both envelopes and nested decisions so a future planning field fails; the horizon-entry seam named in-test at the clocked-mission->:mission hydrator path -- the same seam D10 is landing on, which is the right convergence. Reviewer addition per the live-pin rule: 9d17fb92 pins the allowlist against live record e-0f2f9aec's verbatim body keys (allowlist minus :mission = exactly what the recorder persists; :mission absent = D10's finding kept as history). 21 tests / 78 assertions green after addition. R13 on the U10 matrix moves from missing to covered."
/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/zaif-harness/worklist.edn:141:   :review "Reviewed 2026-09-03 from a clean tree (only untracked runs/build-loop.{log,lock}); work seat was codex per runs/build-loop.log, so author != reviewer. Read both diffs: futon3c 3a5dfcd8 is test-only, one file, +59 lines; futon2 c2ad53f touches only runs/U10-node-coverage.edn and this row; 44c887c is a separate no-amend follow-up. All path-scoped. 3a5dfcd8 is an ancestor of futon3c master. Gates re-run at the delivered sha in an isolated sibling worktree (/home/joe/code/futon3c-review-loop, created from 3a5dfcd8, removed after), never against the live JVM; exit codes captured directly, not through a pipe: clj-kondo exit 0, \"errors: 0, warnings: 0\"; futon4/dev/check-parens.el via arxana-check-parens-cli exit 0, \"OK\"; clojure -M:test -n futon3c.agents.zai-memory-tool-contract-test exit 0, \"Ran 17 tests containing 69 assertions. 0 failures, 0 errors.\" -- the 17/69 in the row reproduces exactly. LIVE PIN checked against the substrate, not just re-run: fixture futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/U12-c-mis-falsifier/node-fixtures/0a18c4f7-R2.edn is git-tracked (git ls-files --error-unmatch confirms), carries :run/id \"0a18c4f7-758e-400a-8223-9c52edf07450\" -- the id cited in the test comment -- and that id also names the harvest source holes/labs/wm-contract/tick-run-record-2026-09-02-0a18c4f7-758e-400a-8223-9c52edf07450.edn, which is UNTRACKED -- but the test never reads it, only the tracked fixture, so no SKIP guard is owed. The three pinned values are verbatim from the fixture (:coupling-density 0.4666666666666667, :mission-health 0.023376623376623377, :stack-pct 0.9968474148802018) and the :value map has exactly 14 keys, which is the \"S7 records 14 real WM channels\" clause of the old :gap now consumed rather than merely noted. No SKIP guard is required because the fixture is tracked; the path is resolved by walking up from io/resource to the deps.edn parent, so it survives a sibling worktr