worklist.edn-245-   :review "Reviewed 2026-09-03 by the build-loop review seat (NOT the author of either half: 623c2969 is claude-2's emergency fix, already independently read by claude-1; ca6884b5 is the work seat's). Diff read for both shas. Gates REPRODUCED in isolated sibling worktree futon3c-review-d13 at ca6884b5, exit codes captured directly, never against the live JVM: clj-kondo 0 errors/0 warnings (one pre-existing info at http.clj:7169, far from the diff), exit 0; check-parens OK, exit 0; futon3c.transport.invoke-ledger-atomicity-test 8 tests/29 assertions, 0 failures, exit 0 -- the claimed numbers exactly. LIVE PIN VERIFIED against /tmp/futon3c-invoke-jobs.edn (read-only file read): job invoke-1787750995295-1507-0f434f39 -- all four values the test calls verbatim match the live record (:state \"failed\", :created-at 2026-08-26T13:29:55.295079374Z, :finished-at 2026-08-26T13:29:56.668288653Z, :event-seq 5); the fixture's event bodies are synthetic bulk and are not claimed as verbatim. Retention logic checked by hand, not just by test: parked-on/snapshot :index holds STILL-AWAITED deps and ensure! is a pure lazy disk load with no resume side effects, so composing compaction into swap-vals! is idempotent under CAS retry and safe inside the writer lock; a terminal job with :finished-at nil is never compacted (conservative -- the zombie case from this very incident); re-compacting an already-compacted job is a fixpoint. ENUMERATION CHECKED rather than taken on trust: grep -n \"!invoke-jobs-ledger\" src/futon3c/transport/http.clj confirms every mutation site is the two update fns plus resets, so \"every atomic ledger update\" holds; the cited line ranges 327-385, 538-540, 564-587 all resolve correctly. I enumerated the 81 distinct top-level job keys in the live ledger against compact-terminal-job's whitelist and traced every dropped key that code reads: :bell-type and :ref are read only for the job being executed (non-terminal), :inbox-path only on the \"delive