ix could not be belled): the outage RECURRED at 19:26 (pool crept to 4.277/4.295GB; even 25.7MB no longer fit; deeper trimming a losing race), so persist-invoke-jobs-ledger! now writes in 1MB chunks (futon3c 623c2969), capping every thread's NIO scratch at 1MB permanently; regression test round-trips a ~3MB ledger (7/23 green with the atomicity suite); transport.http reloaded; persist :ok from a fresh thread; U14b re-dispatched and accepted. INDEPENDENT REVIEW of the self-authored fix: claude-1, ~19:35 (after-the-fact second read closing the author!=reviewer gap the emergency opened): chunk loop correct (wrap-with-offset/len, inner while for partial writes), atomicity structure preserved (tmp + TRUNCATE_EXISTING + force + rename guard + stage hook untouched), cap reasoning matches the NIO mechanism -- clean pass, carve-out use textbook. End-to-end confirmation rides the wm loop's U17 review retry (held through the outage, iterations 13-32, fresh attempt 19:21:55 through the repaired path); claude-1 calls the interim closed when it completes. REMAINING SCOPE: the rolling-expiry half (bound ledger growth; parked/active ids provably retained) -- now an ordinary packet, not an emergency."
