/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/zaif-harness/runs/build-loop.log:4788:    :statement "Agency invoke-jobs ledger: unbounded growth + whole-file direct-buffer persist = dispatch outage (found live 2026-09-02 ~18:50 when two D9 dispatches 500'd with 'invoke-jobs ledger persistence failed'; diagnosed in-JVM via proof-eval). Mechanism: /tmp/futon3c-invoke-jobs.edn is 170MB (every job embeds its full packet text; no effective rolling expiry), and persist-invoke-jobs-ledger! (transport/http.clj:325-375) pr-strs the WHOLE ledger and writes it as ONE FileChannel write -- NIO caches a direct buffer of that size PER THREAD, so the 4GB MaxDirectMemory pool exhausted (4.18/4.29GB allocated); threads holding a cached buffer still persist (ledger mtime kept moving), new threads OOM -- an intermittent-looking global bell outage. Two fixes, both wanted: (a) chunk the channel write (~1MB slices) so no giant direct buffers are ever needed; (b) real rolling expiry/compaction of the ledger (drop aged completed jobs' event texts, keep ids+states; parked jobs' ids must survive). Interim relief needs either a park-aware ledger trim (operator call) or a JVM restart (Joe's call by policy). RELIEF EXECUTED 2026-09-02 ~19:10 (Joe's ruling, relayed by claude-1: 'clean up the log'): 170MB file backed up to /tmp/futon3c-invoke-jobs.edn.bak-20260902-1900; atom trimmed first then persisted once -- 7,454 old terminal jobs slimmed (events -> first/last sans :text/:output/:previews/:tools; :result-text dropped; :events-trimmed :d13/compaction-20260902 marker), 129 kept full (since 17:00Z + running/queued + parked-awaiting); 167MB -> 25.6MB on disk. Verified end to end: probe bell accepted AND its auto-bellback delivered; D9 re-dispatched successfully. Residual: threads holding old 170MB cached direct buffers keep them until thread death, so headroom is improved, not clean. CODE FIX, CHUNKED-WRITE HALF, LANDED 2026-09-02 ~19:30 (claude-2 directly -- carve-out: dispatch was the broken thing, so the fix could not be belled): the outage RECURRED at 19:26 (pool crept to 4.277/4.295GB; even 25.7MB no longer fit; deeper trimming a losing race), so persist-invoke-jobs-ledger! now writes in 1MB chunks (futon3c 623c2969), capping every thread's NIO scratch at 1MB permanently; regression test round-trips a ~3MB ledger (7/23 green with the atomicity suite); transport.http reloaded; persist :ok from a fresh thread; U14b re-dispatched and accepted. INDEPENDENT REVIEW of the self-authored fix: claude-1, ~19:35 (after-the-fact second read closing the author!=reviewer gap the emergency opened): chunk loop correct (wrap-with-offset/len, inner while for partial writes), atomicity structure preserved (tmp + TRUNCATE_EXISTING + force + rename guard + stage hook untouched), cap reasoning matches the NIO mechanism -- clean pass, carve-out use textbook. End-to-end confirmation rides the wm loop's U17 review retry (held through the outage, iterations 13-32, fresh attempt 19:21:55 through the repaired path); claude-1 calls the interim closed when it completes. REMAINING SCOPE: the rolling-expiry half (bound ledger growth; parked/active ids provably retained) -- now an ordinary packet, not an emergency."
