/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/zaif-harness/runs/build-loop.log-18703-holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn:346:   :review "Re-ran the experiment myself; every number reproduces. edn/read in a loop confirmed in read-forms; the rank-proxy limit is stated wherever a rank appears; derived predictions are labelled derived. THE RESULT: the arms differ on every field/start combination (14-36 transitions), the argmax never moves anywhere, and the carry stays in 0.28..5.58, nowhere near either solver bound. ONE HEADLINE CLAIM DOES NOT SURVIVE. The report reads July 4 forgetting its initial beta while July 5 stays path-dependent as a difference between the FIELDS. It is a difference in SEQUENCE LENGTH. At t=17, the transition count where 07-05 ends, the four 07-04 trajectories are still fully separated -- 0.4977, 0.8698, 1.5757, 2.4844 for beta_0 of 0.5, 1, 2, 5 -- exactly like 07-05. The collapse to ~0.453 happens between t=17 and t=37, which 07-05 does not have. Both fields retain path dependence at 17 transitions; only one has enough transitions to lose it. The comparison was made at two different sequence lengths, which is the AGENTS.md rule failing in the mirror direction: two things compared at different values of the parameter that governs the effect. THE TRAJECTORY IS NOT A SMOOTH DECAY either: from beta_0 = 5 on 07-04 it falls to 2.48 by t=18, JUMPS to 3.58 at t=19, decays to 1.19 by t=26, jumps to 2.85 at t=27, then decays to 0.45. Something in the field pushes beta up twice. Four trajectories landing within 0.001 at t=37 is real contraction, but it takes more than twenty ticks to show. WHY THIS MATTERS FOR R2, which is the point of having run it now: the planned validation run is about 20 ticks, and on this evidence a carried beta over 20 ticks is still dominated by its beta_0. R2 will NOT show the carry learning anything, and a reader expecting it to will misread a length limit as a null result. RUN2 report must state its beta_0 and tick count beside any beta number and must not call a 20-tick carry converged. THE RULING IS NOT CONTRADICTED. Carrying and resetting give different orderings everywhere tested, so the choice is real; it simply never reaches the top of the ranking on these fields, and the horizon over which carrying accumulates is longer than either recorded field. Recorded beside the ruling in :choices :gamma-fixed-point per Joe rule, with no ruling edited. METHOD NOTE AGAINST MYSELF: I read my own results file with edn/read-string, got one form of sixteen, and reported 16 rows as 18 keys before catching it -- fourth instance today of a tool returning part of a thing and being read as the whole, and the first where the AGENTS.md rule caught me rather than someone else."
/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/zaif-harness/runs/build-loop.log-18704-holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn:360:   :review "Read against registry 27ab9c7, tree clean. RE-RAN THE EXPERIMENT (clojure -M c464_beta_carry_experiment.clj, 16 forms read with edn/read in a loop): argmax-change ticks 0 across all 16 arm/field/start forms; carried beta min 0.2814 max 5.5766; carried differs from fixed on 18/35/36/35 of 37 transitions (07-04) and 15/14/15/14 of 17 (07-05); 07-04 carried finals 0.4529/0.4530/0.4532/0.4538 for beta_0 0.5/1/2/5; every tick :bracketed and :converged. Every number in :run-result reproduces. The length-not-field correction (t=17 separation 0.4977/0.8698/1.5757/2.4844 vs t=37 contraction to ~0.453) is in the C464 table at line 132 and is the right reading; its consequence for RUN2 -- report beta_0 and tick count beside every beta, never call a 20-tick carry converged -- belongs in R2 acceptance. Ruling not contradicted; recorded beside it as Joe rule asks." :owner :claude-20
