{:id :D13 :class :I :status :done :owner :any :covers-key :none
   :reviewed-by "zaif-build-loop/claude-review"
   :reviewed-at "2026-09-03T05:52:26Z"
   :review "Reviewed 2026-09-03 by the build-loop review seat (NOT the author of either half: 623c2969 is claude-2's emergency fix, already independently read by claude-1; ca6884b5 is the work seat's). Diff read for both shas. Gates REPRODUCED in isolated sibling worktree futon3c-review-d13 at ca6884b5, exit codes captured directly, never against the live JVM: clj-kondo 0 errors/0 warnings (one pre-existing info at http.clj:7169, far from the diff), exit 0; check-parens OK, exit 0; futon3c.transport.invoke-ledger-atomicity-test 8 tests/29 assertions, 0 failures, exit 0 -- the claimed numbers exactly. LIVE PIN VERIFIED against /tmp/futon3c-invoke-jobs.edn (read-only file read): job invoke-1787750995295-1507-0f434f39 -- all four values the test calls verbatim match the live record (:state \"failed\", :created-at 2026-08-26T13:29:55.295079374Z, :finished-at 2026-08-26T13:29:56.668288653Z, :event-seq 5); the fixture's event bodies are synthetic bulk and are not claimed as verbatim. Retention logic checked by hand, not just by test: parked-on/snapshot :index holds STILL-AWAITED deps and ensure! is a pure lazy disk load with no resume side effects, so composing compaction into swap-vals! is idempotent under CAS retry and safe inside the writer lock; a terminal job with :finished-at nil is never compacted (conservative -- the zombie case from this very incident); re-compacting an already-compacted job is a fixpoint. ENUMERATION CHECKED rather than taken on trust: grep -n \"!invoke-jobs-ledger\" src/futon3c/transport/http.clj confirms every mutation site is the two update fns plus resets, so \"every atomic ledger update\" holds; the cited line ranges 327-385, 538-540, 564-587 all resolve correctly. I enumerated the 81 distinct top-level job keys in the live ledger against compact-terminal-job's whitelist and traced every dropped key that code reads: :bell-type and :ref are read only for the job being executed (non-terminal), :inbox-path only on the \"delivered\" state (non-terminal), so no reader breaks. ONE FINDING, FIXED BY THE REVIEWER (futon3c ae88efe7, path-scoped): invoke-job-public-view (http.clj:1698-1706) did not expose :events-trimmed, so GET /api/alpha/invoke/jobs/<id> on a compacted job returned :result nil with nothing to distinguish an expired transcript from a job that never produced a result -- the silent-degradation shape this board keeps typing (cf. D8 micro-finding (a)). Fix adds the key to the view plus an assertion; NEGATIVE CONTROL run: the assertion fails with nil against the unpatched view, so it guards something real. Post-fix in the same isolated worktree: 8 tests/30 assertions green, kondo 0/0, parens OK, all exit 0. TWO RESIDUALS, typed not papered, neither blocking: (a) OUTSTANDING ACCEPTANCE -- \"live JVM reload recorded\" is NOT met and cannot be met by this loop (the review seat is forbidden the live JVM and the work seat deferred it by row protocol); the lane owner still owes the acceptance reload from /home/joe/code/futon3c master, and until then the expiry is code-only, not relief; (b) the expiry bounds per-record DETAIL (<2000 chars per tombstone, asserted) but not record COUNT -- 7,594 jobs of tombstone is still ~15MB and grows monotonically, so the ledger is bounded in the sense the row asked for and unbounded in another. Also noted: compaction overwrites the manual pass's :d13/compaction-20260902 provenance marker with :d13/rolling-expiry (cosmetic), and the 623c2969 chunk test proves a 3MB ledger round-trips but not that the write was chunked (a single write would also pass) -- the chunking itself rests on claude-1's read of the loop."
   :lane "claude-2"
   :evidence "futon3c 623c2969 (landed chunked-write half, independently reviewed and live-reloaded as recorded in the statement) + ca6884b5 (rolling 24h terminal-detail expiry). The latter compacts at both startup and every atomic ledger update (src/futon3c/transport/http.clj:327-385,538-540,564-587), preserves every job id/state, retains all nonterminal jobs and terminal jobs still named by parked-on's durable dependency index, and bounds expired terminal records to identity/state metadata plus first/last event edges. Test test/futon3c/transport/invoke_ledger_atomicity_test.clj:194 pins verbatim live job invoke-1787750995295-1507-0f434f39 and proves old detail bounded while active/parked detail survives. Gates: clj-kondo 0 errors/0 warnings; check-parens OK; futon3c.transport.invoke-ledger-atomicity-test 8 tests/29 assertions green. No live reload by WORK seat, per row protocol; lane owner performs acceptance reload. Post-repair bell success is already recorded in the statement."
   :statement "Agency invoke-jobs ledger: unbounded growth + whole-file direct-buffer persist = dispatch outage (found live 2026-09-02 ~18:50 when two D9 dispatches 500'd with 'invoke-jobs ledger persistence failed'; diagnosed in-JVM via proof-eval). Mechanism: /tmp/futon3c-invoke-jobs.edn is 170MB (every job embeds its full packet text; no effective rolling expiry), and persist-invoke-jobs-ledger! (transport/http.clj:325-375) pr-strs the WHOLE ledger and writes it as ONE FileChannel write -- NIO caches a direct buffer of that size PER THREAD, so the 4GB MaxDirectMemory pool exhausted (4.18/4.29GB allocated); threads holding a cached buffer still persist (ledger mtime kept moving), new threads OOM -- an intermittent-looking global bell outage. Two fixes, both wanted: (a) chunk the channel write (~1MB slices) so no giant direct buffers are ever needed; (b) real rolling expiry/compaction of the ledger (drop aged completed jobs' event texts, keep ids+states; parked jobs' ids must survive). Interim relief needs either a park-aware ledger trim (operator call) or a JVM restart (Joe's call by policy). RELIEF EXECUTED 2026-09-02 ~19:10 (Joe's ruling, relayed by claude-1: 'clean up the log'): 170MB file backed up to /tmp/futon3c-invoke-jobs.edn.bak-20260902-1900; atom trimmed first then persisted once -- 7,454 old terminal jobs slimmed (events -> first/last sans :text/:output/:previews/:tools; :result-text dropped; :events-trimmed :d13/compaction-20260902 marker), 129 kept full (since 17:00Z + running/queued + parked-awaiting); 167MB -> 25.6MB on disk. Verified end to end: probe bell accepted AND its auto-bellback delivered; D9 re-dispatched successfully. Residual: threads holding old 170MB cached direct buffers keep them until thread death, so headroom is improved, not clean. CODE FIX, CHUNKED-WRITE HALF, LANDED 2026-09-02 ~19:30 (claude-2 directly -- carve-out: dispatch was the broken thing, so the fix could not be belled): the outage RECURRED at 19:26 (pool crept to 4.277