ucture now; I’ll turn this into a concrete “thin build now, AIF semantics preserved” amendment rather than leaving it as a conceptual aside.\n\nThe paper currently overclaims the seam: it equates “queryable” with “remembered,” and says R16 follows almost automatically from immutability. The live store disproves the first claim, while R16 requires an independently witnessed outcome. I’m tightening that language and making pattern-conditioned recall the R6 bridge.\n\nThe paper currently overclaims the seam: it equates “queryable” with “remembered,” and says R16 follows almost automatically from immutability. The live store disproves the first claim, while R16 requires an independently witnessed outcome. I’m tightening that language and making pattern-conditioned recall the R6 bridge.\n\nThe documents now separate three claims that had been collapsed: recorded, retrieved, and independently shown useful. I’ve also preserved zai-3’s direct-build route: P1 can start as a thin `psr_search`/`psr_select` enrichment without waiting for a full EFE controller or Librarian. I’m doing a final consistency check on the wording and LaTeX.\n\nThe documents now separate three claims that had been collapsed: recorded, retrieved, and independently shown useful. I’ve also preserved zai-3’s direct-build route: P1 can start as a thin `psr_search`/`psr_select` enrichment without waiting for a full EFE controller or Librarian. I’m doing a final consistency check on the wording and LaTeX.\n\nI’ve adapted the memory work around the AIF story.\n\nThe central distinction is now:\n\n- A memory is a typed R2 observation.\n- A pattern is an R6 policy hypothesis and retrieval handle.\n- Memory–pattern attachment is a revisable claim.\n- Applying a memory does not validate it; only an independently witnessed result provides R16 grounding.\n\nI updated:\n\n- [CODEX-HANDOFF-p0-memory-record.md](/home/joe/code/futon3c/holes/CODEX-HANDOFF-p0-memory-record.md)\n- [M-typed-memories.md](/home/joe/code/futon3c/holes/missions/M-typed-memories.md)\n- [main-2026.tex](/home/joe/code/p4ng/main-2026.tex)\n\nThe proposed direct P1 build is now:\n\n`task → R6 pattern candidates → attached supporting/challenging memories → selection citing memory IDs → action → external outcome → R3/R7 update`\n\nThis addresses the concrete live problem: the stored memories currently have no pattern endpoints, so lexical searchability does not make them operationally retrievable.\n\nI also corrected the paper’s stale claims that writes were still only designed and that R16 followed nearly automatically from immutable storage. The paper now distinguishes “recorded,” “retrieved,” and “worked.”\n\n`main-2026.tex` builds successfully with `latexmk`. No commits were made; the two futon3c documents were already untracked.\n\nI’ve adapted the memory work around the AIF story.\n\nThe central distinction is now:\n\n- A memory is a typed R2 observation.\n- A pattern is an R6 policy hypothesis and retrieval handle.\n- Memory–pattern attachment is a revisable claim.\n- Applying a memory does not validate it; only an independently witnessed result provides R16 grounding.\n\nI updated:\n\n- [CODEX-HANDOFF-p0-memory-record.md](/home/joe/code/futon3c/holes/CODEX-HANDOFF-p0-memory-record.md)\n- [M-typed-memories.md](/home/joe/code/futon3c/holes/missions/M-typed-memories.md)\n- [main-2026.tex](/home/joe/code/p4ng/main-2026.tex)\n\nThe proposed direct P1 build is now:\n\n`task → R6 pattern candidates → attached supporting/challenging memories → selection citing memory IDs → action → external outcome → R3/R7 update`\n\nThis addresses the concrete live problem: the stored memories currently have no pattern endpoints, so lexical searchability does not make them operationally retrievable.\n\nI also corrected the paper’s stale claims that writes were still only designed and that R16 followed nearly automatically from immutable storage. The paper now distinguishes “recorded,” “retrieved,” and “worked.”\n\n`main-2026.tex` builds successfully with `latexmk`. No commits were made; the two futon3c documents were already untracked.\n\nTOOL DIGEST\n{:kind :custom_tool_call, :name \"exec\", :call-id \"call_pzIUSRg5l0I9ZByU1Sj3DO6S\", :args \"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\\\"rg -n -A16 -B3 '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\label\\\\\\\\{def:R1[7-9]\\\\\\\\}|\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\label\\\\\\\\{def:R20\\\\\\\\}|R17|Structure learning|structure learning' main-2026.tex\\\",\\\"workdir\\\":\\\"/home/joe/code/p4ng\\\",\\\"yi…\"}\n{:kind :custom_tool_call_output, :call-id \"call_pzIUSRg5l0I9ZByU1Sj3DO6S\", :output \"Script completed Wall time 0.1 seconds Output: Warning: truncated output (original token count: 8725) Total output lines: 142 472- 473-\\\\paragraph{Embedding space.} An embedding turns text into a point…\"}\n{:kind :custom_tool_call, :name \"exec\", :call-id \"call_CvNCazSSmXEyY8nXwRXEF7jl\", :args \"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\\\"sed -n '526,550p' main-2026.tex\\\",\\\"workdir\\\":\\\"/home/joe/code/p4ng\\\",\\\"yield_time_ms\\\":10000,\\\"max_output_tokens\\\":6000}); text(r.output) \"}\n{:kind :custom_tool_call_output, :call-id \"call_CvNCazSSmXEyY8nXwRXEF7jl\", :output \"Script completed Wall time 0.1 seconds Output: \\\\subsubsection*{Learning, planning, and closing the loop (R12--R17)} \\\\paragraph{Two-Layer Calibration (R12).} \\\\textbf{If} predicted-versus-realised pairs…\"}\n{:kind :custom_tool_call, :name \"exec\", :call-id \"call_pxhALIwMDShYNvnyz0KJE43K\", :args \"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\\\"sed -n '1,260p' holes/CODEX-HANDOFF-p0-memory-record.md && git status --short -- holes/CODEX-HANDOFF-p0-memory-record.md holes/missions/M-typed-memories.md\\\",\\\"w…\"}\n{:kind :custom_tool_call_output, :call-id \"call_pxhALIwMDShYNvnyz0KJE43K\", :output \"Script completed Wall time 0.1 seconds Output: # CODEX-HANDOFF — P0 `memory_record`: a Zai runner can write a memory Mission: `holes/missions/M-typed-memories.md` (DERIVE, prototype ladder rung P0). P…\"}\n{:ki