tion gates. I’ll resume there—no rerun of the runner trial or duplicate live writes.\n\nYes. The live Phase 2 acceptance itself completed before the timeout; I was at the final verification and documentation gates. I’ll resume there—no rerun of the runner trial or duplicate live writes.\n\nPhase 2 is finished and accepted live.\n\nThe complete path worked:\n\n`psr_search → psr_select → full memory recall → theorem application → independent Lean check → PUR/use receipt`\n\nKey evidence:\n\n- Runner: `zai-6`\n- PSR: `psr-9fbf1e64-3104-4757-813f-756e1864c871`\n- Used earlier-session memory: `e-6bcbb51e-f368-4bcc-afbf-97fcc616772d`\n- Independent checker outcome: `e-c830f282-b5fe-4475-bde7-c4a18246c441`\n- Final PUR: `pur-925e34b4-326e-42e2-956f-d304ef00bed0`\n- Final structured receipt: `e-f7c2532b-d6a0-4744-a0c8-945e0c45f596`\n\nThe receipt distinguishes all three recalled memories:\n\n- one used;\n- one explicitly rejected as irrelevant;\n- one left unused;\n- all linked to the separately authored checker outcome.\n\nThe live trial is [FutonPhase2MemoryTrial.lean](/home/joe/code/apm-lean/FutonPhase2MemoryTrial.lean). Independent `lake env lean` validation passed; SHA-256 is `6cbcaf350b3f5f08063d540adf23798b4adf1a526556c2e47c447b0b3de3775b`.\n\nThe run discovered and repaired two real boundary defects:\n\n- prediction-error prose was incompatible with the PUR’s structured field;\n- reason maps keyed by evidence IDs were stringified by the HTTP backend.\n\nBoth now survive direct store read-back structurally.\n\nOne important residual remains: the natural semantic query did not retrieve the intended pattern; an ID-like query did. That prediction error is persisted and becomes a Phase 3 candidate-construction issue—without introducing an embedding fallback prematurely.\n\nDocumentation is updated in:\n\n- [M-shared-memory-control-build-test.md](/home/joe/code/futon3c/holes/missions/M-shared-memory-control-build-test.md)\n- [M-typed-memories.md](/home/joe/code/futon3c/ho