 `lpNorm`]", :clocked-target "E-memory-topology", :excursion-id "E-memory-topology", :clocked-excursion "E-memory-topology"}, :session-id "4fc6f9c2-1807-40ac-8721-d38eb588cfe9", :tags [:claude :chat :turn :assistant], :at "2026-07-31T04:26:21.365648175Z", :type :coordination, :subject #:ref{:type :session, :id "4fc6f9c2-1807-40ac-8721-d38eb588cfe9"}, :author "claude-9", :claim-type :observation, :id "emacs-97988bfc580bbf9cac51e01e5717cd0a"}}], :count 5, :checked 5, :index-as-of "2026-07-31T04:44:43.940884560Z"}, :proposal-rows [], :validation-projection {:ok true, :groups []}, :pattern-projection {:ok true, :groups []}, :capture-audit {:search-row-count 5, :proposal-row-count 0, :memory-row-count 0, :description-pattern-count 0, :attached-pattern-count 0}}} {:status :captured, :case {:case-id "hard-problems-a97a06-lean-main-lean", :query "analytic complex analyticon line", :query-provenance {:problem "hard-problems-a97a06-lean-main-lean", :job-id "invoke-1785470492377-469-c4cbe680", :offered-evidence-id "e-1440bd64-7c38-4068-ad9c-a83e49a9c23e", :receipt-at "2026-07-31T04:01:33.457108089Z", :selection-rule :latest-recorded-query-per-problem}, :search-result {:results [{:score -23.036622637547655, :entry #:evidence{:body {:event :turn-round, :text "Good. Let me think about the approach more carefully. \n\nThe identity theorem `AnalyticOnNhd.eqOn_of_preconnected_of_eventuallyEq` could be useful. But the key challenge is constructing `g`.\n\nLet me think about a different, more concrete approach. For the specific function `apm_a96J10_f`, the evenness `apm_a96J10_f_even` is already proven. Instead of the abstract factoring theorem, maybe I should try to construct `g` concretely.\n\nActually wait - the theorem `apm_a96J10_main` already depends on `apm_a96J10_even_factors`. So I need to prove `apm_a96J10_even_factors` for the pipeline to work.\n\nLet me think about the most Mathlib-idiomatic approach. The key insight: for complex functions, I can use the Cauchy integral fo