**\n\n**Planning exterior connectivity construction**\n**Searching isPathConnected_compl_singleton**\n\n**Searching path connectedness of punctured ball**\n\n**Formalizing exterior path connectivity**\n**Planning lemma proof with radial paths**\n\n**Formulating generic componentSet scratch**\n\n**Identifying closure misuse**\n\n**Verifying interior membership in topology**\n\n**Resolving ambiguity in isOpen field usage**\n\n**Defining representative function with quotient mapping**\n\n**Proving bounded sublevel sets using isProperMap**\n\n**Verifying preimage compactness**\n\n**Planning proof for superlevel connectedness**\n\n**Proving super component equality and exterior path connectedness**\n\n**Constructing exterior path using scaled points**\n**Exploring annulus path connectedness lemma**\n\n**Planning topology lemma audit**\n\n\n\n**Retrieving abstract from database**\n\n**Advancing partial lemniscate component proof**\n**Adding lemniscate closure and boundedness lemmas**\n\n**Removing error-causing check line**\n\n**Checking equivalence of aeval and eval**\n\n**Simplifying norm and dist expressions**\n\n**Planning helper integration and imports**\n**Establishing component set classification lemmas**\n\n**Adding meaningful partial patch**\n\n**Compiling codebase**\n\n**Recalling precise error details**\n\n**Fixing explicit binder usage in lemmas**\n**Clarifying explicit hp binder necessity and isClosed_eq use**\n\n**Adding type annotations for continuity proof**\n\n**Compiling inferred componentSet_open signature**\n\n**Inspecting specific code line**\n\n**Adding hp binder to lemma and revising super lemma**\n\n**Assessing finite cardinal bounds**\n**Characterizing collinear segment endpoints**\n\n**Defining continuous radial projection map**\n**Prototyping lemma for radial map inverse**\n\nAGENT MESSAGES\nI’m starting by checking what topology and polynomial-growth infrastructure the file has already built. Mathematically, the complement of a polynomial lemniscate is usually the basin of infinity and is connected; the stated degree-plus-one bound may therefore be deliberately weaker than the natural theorem. I’ll verify that against the scaffold before choosing the formal route.\n\nI’m starting by checking what topology and polynomial-growth infrastructure the file has already built. Mathematically, the complement of a polynomial lemniscate is usually the basin of infinity and is connected; the stated degree-plus-one bound may therefore be deliberately weaker than the natural theorem. I’ll verify that against the scaffold before choosing the formal route.\n\nThe bounded-component half is now formalizable with current APIs: open components have frontier in the lemniscate, sublevel components are bounded by properness of polynomial evaluation, and the existing minimum-modulus lemma puts a root in each such component. The remaining genuinely separate issue is the one-endedness of the plane needed to identify all unbounded superlevel components; I’m isolating that boundary rather than conflating it with component bookkeeping.\n\nThe bounded-component half is now formalizable with current APIs: open components have frontier in the lemniscate, sublevel components are bounded by properness of polynomial evaluation, and the existing minimum-modulus lemma puts a root in each such component. The remaining genuinely separate issue is the one-endedness of the plane needed to identify all unbounded superlevel components; I’m isolating that boundary rather than conflating it with component bookkeeping.\n\nTOOL DIGEST\n{:kind :function_call, :name \"exec_command\", :call-id \"call_NIXMawXtSkJDrC2pwSXjfuDo\", :args \"{\\\"cmd\\\":\\\"cat /home/joe/code/AGENTS.md; sed -n '1,380p' problems/a00J04/lean/Main.lean; git status --short\\\",\\\"workdir\\\":\\\"/home/joe/code/apm-lean\\\",\\\"yield_time_ms\\\":10000,\\\"max_output_tokens\\\":30000}\"}\n{:kind :function_call_output, :call-id \"call_NIXMawXtSkJDrC2pwSXjfuDo\", :output \"Chunk ID: