R8’s clean seam is a two-test data contract in the existing ZAIF input namespace: one test turns the absence of a realised-observation field in a tracked live ZAIF replay into an explicit reason-bearing absence; the other replays the recorded WM R8 prediction-error arithmetic and requires exact zero delta. No production code or live JVM interaction is needed.
