    :acceptance "Per-node unit test(s) closing the matrix :gap; LIVE-PIN rule (>=1 pin from a live or tracked-fixture record, id cited in a comment; untracked data guarded with a visible SKIP); gates clean in own process (clj-kondo 0 errors, check-parens, named test namespaces green); path-scoped commits; the runs/U10-node-coverage.edn entry for this node updated (spec-test status + new test pointers) in the same futon2 commit so U10 stays refreshable."
-   :evidence "futon3c 27a0f6d5: test/futon3c/agents/zai_memory_tool_contract_test.clj:156-236 (all registered runner tools, ask/yield terminal witnesses, and tracked live WM R16 typed absence). futon2 (this commit): runs/U10-node-coverage.edn R16 entry and this row. Gates: clj-kondo 0 errors/0 warnings; check-parens exit 0; clojure -M:test -n futon3c.agents.zai-memory-tool-contract-test, 20 tests/194 assertions green."
+   :evidence "futon3c 27a0f6d5 + repair 44b714ed: test/futon3c/agents/zai_memory_tool_contract_test.clj:156-245 (all registered runner tools, production :zaif dual-decide persisted :ask/:yield arm witnesses at line 178, and tracked live WM R16 typed absence at line 231). futon2 (this commit): runs/U10-node-coverage.edn R16 entry and this row. Gates: clj-kondo 0 errors/0 warnings; check-parens exit 0; clojure -M:test -n futon3c.agents.zai-memory-tool-contract-test, 20 tests/196 assertions green."
    :review-finding "REVIEW FAIL -- the work STANDS, do not revert it; the defect is in one deftest's claim and in the U10 note, not in the code under test. Reviewed at futon3c 27a0f6d5 in an isolated sibling worktree (/home/joe/code/futon3c-review-loop, created at that sha, removed afterwards); the live JVM (:7070/:6768) was never touched and nothing was loaded into it. EVERYTHING THE ROW CLAIMS REPRODUCES, exit codes read directly with no pipe: clj-kondo --lint test/futon3c/agents/zai_memory_tool_contract_test.clj exit 0, 0 errors 0 warnings; futon4/dev/check-parens.sh on the same file exit 0 (OK); clojure -M:test -n futon3c.agents.zai-memory-tool-contract-test exit 0, 20 tests / 194 assertions, 0 failures 0 errors -- the row's numbers are exact. The three new deftests begin at 156, 178 and 222 and the last ends at 236 (the next deftest is at 238), so the U10 pointers and the row's 156-236 range are both right. The R16 pin is real and TRACKED (git ls-files --error-unmatch succeeds on wm-contract/runs/U12-c-mis-falsifier/node-fixtures/801976e7-R16.edn), so no SKIP guard is owed, and I read all six asserted fields out of the file myself: :node :R16, :run/id 801976e7-01c6-4e39-aada-27f620f7c2f1, :via enactment, :basis 'S7: R16 enactment data does not exist until a flight flies', :status :absent, :reason :no-enactment-yet -- and the line-222 pointer carries that :record-id. The deftest at 156 is the real gain and is NOT vacuous: I evaluated the registry off the test classpath and it holds 28 tool names, with (set (map :name @#'zai/tool-specs)) equal to the names from (#'zai/openai-tools :full), so the doseq drives all 28 through the production make-invoke-fn round loop rather than a hand-listed subset. Commits are path-scoped (27a0f6d5: one test file, 65 insertions / 0 deletions; futon2 5d6d9f4: U10-node-coverage.edn + worklist.edn, the worklist hunk confined to this row), and 27a0f6d5 is an ancestor of master sitting directly on U11b c686ca27 with no --amend. THE FINDING: the deftest at 178, runner-ask-and-yield-endings-record-r16-witnesses, does not test ask or yield, and the U10 R16 :shared-machinery :note asserts that it does ('the companion terminal test covers ask/yield endings'). The runner has no ask/yield ending to record -- grep -rniE '(^|[^a-z])(ask|yield|ending|terminal)([^a-z]|$)' src/futon3c/agents/zai_api.clj, run untruncated over all 1516 lines, returns ZERO lines. Both iterations of that deftest run the identical production path (one round, no tool calls) and differ only in the assistant string the zai/chat! stub returns; the :ask and :yield keywords are then re-derived inside the test by a case form that maps 'Need operator input' back to :ask and 'Yielding control' back to :yield. What the assertions do establish is worth keeping and is not covered elsewhere in the file -- a round with no tool calls still records a :turn-round witness carrying the assistant text and :calls [] -- but that is not an ask/yield ending. The production :ask and :yield that DO exist are arms of zaif-controller/decide (src/futon3c/agents/zaif_controller.clj:100-141, ask-value at :87-94, :yield-baseline at :20), reached from a :zaif-profile turn via zai_api.clj:1153 zaif/dual-decide, and this row's tests assert nothing about the recorded arm. So :gap nil and :spec-test :covered overstate the flip gate: of the recorded gap's three clauses, the memory-family-only clause is genuinely closed (28/28 registered tools) and the no-WM-enactment-datum clause is honestly pinned by the tracked typed absence, but 'not every runner tool/ask/yield is covered' is closed for tools ONLY. TO REPAIR, pick one and keep both good tests: (a) assert the real thing -- the :zaif-profile round already runs dual-decide, so pin the recorded decision arm on the R16 witness and :gap nil becomes true; or (b) restate honestly -- rename the deftest at 178 to what it checks (a no-tool-call round records a :turn-round witness with empty :calls), drop the ask/yield-endings sentence from the U10 note, and leave a residual :gap naming the uncovered ask/yield arm, pointing at test/futon3c/agents/zaif_controller_test.clj:79, :217-259 and :348-378, where those arms ARE covered today (including the recorded finding that the shipped constant makes :ask unreachable) -- just not at R16. Either way the row's :evidence should stop describing line 178 as 'ask/yield terminal witnesses'. MINOR, not blocking (the same caveat U18z-U21z carry): workspace-root resolves to /home/joe/code and the fixture is slurped from the futon2 WORKING TREE, so the pin reads whatever revision futon2 is checked out at rather than 5d6d9f4, and it throws rather than SKIPs if futon2 is absent."}
