/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn:727:   :evidence "futon2 845de41 (the test ns, the probe, its artifact, C489, and the M-zaif-harness note) and the ledger commit carrying this line. WHAT WAS BUILT: test/futon2/aif/zaif_full_loop_test.clj, 620 lines, 15 deftests / 136 assertions, ONE deftest per R node so a regression names the node. THE CROSS-REPO PROBLEM AND HOW IT IS CLOSED, because it is the first thing a reviewer will doubt: zaif v0 lives in futon3c (src/futon3c/agents/zaif_controller.clj L1-L270, zaif_inputs.clj L1-L209) and futon3c is NOT on futon2's classpath (futon2/deps.edn L1-L8, the :deps map), so a futon2 test cannot call decide(). The acceptance permits a planted fixture 'with the shape pinned against zaif_controller.clj'. The fixture's NUMBERS are not planted: they were produced by the SHIPPED controller by u6_zaif_decision.clj:1-109 running in the futon3c JVM against futon3c 0252995, frozen at U6-ZAIF-DECISION.txt (byte-identical on two consecutive runs, md5 bc7764596e6769a5928763850db93e7b). The fixture's SHAPE is re-derived from the controller SOURCE on every test run: controller-forms (zaif_full_loop_test.clj:94-104) reads the file, source-constants and source-arm-order pull the constants map and the arm vector, and zaif-fixture-shape-is-pinned-against-the-controller-source-test (:261-289) checks the fixture against both. VERIFIED BY MUTATION IN BOTH DIRECTIONS: changing the FIXTURE's operator-attention-cost 0.65 -> 0.5 turns the suite red (3 failures), and changing the SOURCE constant 0.65 -> 0.55 turns it red the same way (futon3c working tree restored to clean immediately after; git status empty). That is what z2_calibrate.clj L56-L58's self-declared inlined copy of the arithmetic does not have. THE FROZEN DECISION is a real recorded operator turn, e-ce907fcf-c7e1-4272-a4a2-13def7aaaa50 at 2026-06-08T15:26:51.274850972Z from calibration-sessions.edn: gold-judged, :is_correction true, attributed to M-futon-forward-model -- the ONE mission whose B1 gamma cell is burned in (gamma 0.7071067811865476, not the uniform 1.0), so the fixture is non-degenerate on the gamma channel. Its decision is :arm :retrieve, g-terms {:retrieve 0.7622675616071356 :act 0.0 :ask 0.35 :yield 0.0}. TWO FINDINGS ABOUT THE SHIPPED CONTROLLER, measured over ALL 114 recorded sessions replayed through the live hydrator, not inferred. (1) GAMMA IS READ ON EVERY DECISION AND ENTERS NONE OF THEM: gamma-for-mission (zaif_controller.clj L34-L44) is consulted every time and its only consumer is act-value (L76-L85), whose belief term falls back to 0.0 because the live hydrator sets :task-belief {} unconditionally (zaif_inputs.clj L190-L194). The :act G-term is EXACTLY 0.0 on 114 of 114 sessions, so gamma multiplies zero. Joe's 'recorded but never consulted' one level down: not merely unread, read into a product with a structurally absent factor. (2) 83 OF 114 LIVE DECISIONS WERE SETTLED BY THE TIE ORDER, NOT BY A SCORE: with :act and :yield both at 0.0 they tie at the maximum whenever :retrieve and :ask are both <= 0, and choose-arm's explicit (case arm :act 0 ...) key (zaif_controller.clj L98-L103) takes :act. Only the 31 :retrieve choices were settled by arithmetic. Same shape as the ZU-2 ':ask is structurally unreachable' finding, one arm over and now with the denominator. At the Z3a sweep cost 0.15 the distribution becomes {:ask 99 :retrieve 15} and :act disappears entirely. WHAT IS PLANTED, AND THE CONTROL THAT SAYS HOW MUCH IT CARRIES. zaif v0 declares NO observation model -- its arm values are dimensionless preference scores -- so ANY placement of them into the WM's observation space is a declared choice, not a derivation. Exactly two things are planted: the per-arm Q(o|pi) at R4 and the realised observation at R8. The plant is made in ONE function, plant-per-arm-prediction (zaif_full_loop_test.clj:152-167), whose docstring states the rule and calls the addition dimensionally arbitrary. plant-dependence-negative-control-test (:539-562) runs the same three arms on three plant channels and gets THREE DIFFERENT R5 orderings -- :mission-health [:ask :act :retrieve], :support-coverage [:act :retrieve :ask], :sorry-count-norm [:act :ask :retrieve] -- and two different head-law choices. So which arm the WM prefers is a property of the plant and NOT of the arms, and nothing here may be read as a measurement of which arm is right. One further thing is FORCED rather than measured and the test says so at the assertion (:433-440): every planted mean is base + a non-negative G-term and the realised value IS base, so R8's F_pi ordering is monotone in the planted gain by construction. WHAT THE PIPELINE DOES WHEN IT RUNS, flags-on (:selection-law :full-score-posterior, :f-pi-policy-posterior? true), on the :mission-health plant. R5: G = risk + ambiguity with residual EXACTLY 0.0 on all three arms; risk discriminates (3 distinct values) and AMBIGUITY DOES NOT -- one value, -0.883646559789373, on all three, because zaif declares no per-arm variance anywhere in its source, so G's ordering IS the risk ordering exactly. Structurally the same shape C487 found on the WM's own side: the deficiency is the coverage of declared variances, not the functional. R14: tau 0.10396979632561867 from the arm G spread at unit selection gain. R6 ln E is the ONE R6 input that is measured rather than planted -- folded from the recorded arm history (83 :act, 31 :retrieve, 0 :ask) by the WM's own habit-prior/observe-action, so :ask sits at the alpha-only floor, ln E -4.762173934797756. R16: THREE LAWS, THREE ARMS, FROM ONE RECORDED DECISION -- zaif chose :retrieve, the controller-head law chooses :ask, the full-score law chooses :act with :moved-from-controller-head? true, and under this plant the arm zaif chose is the WM's LEAST preferred at G. THE HONEST GAP LIST is data, not narration: r-node-coverage (:564-601) and zaif-r-node-coverage-is-complete-and-typed-test (:603-620) assert that the node set matches the nodes U6's statement names, that every entry is typed and carries a basis pointer, that EXACTLY ONE node (R16) is :exercises, that R5 and R14 are :partial, and that R17 is :stub-by-design -- which is what the statement predicted. R4's stub is pinned by behaviour, not by assertion: forward_model.clj:25-31 excludes all four arms and fm/predict THROWS on each (:332-341). U5 HELD: r16-candidates-stay-opaque-at-the-seam-test (:487-512) gives the same scores, ln E and F_pi to {:type :retrieve} candidates and to :apply-cascade candidates with different targets and payloads, and gets the same chosen rank and the same :selection-law :chosen-rank, while the candidate identity does change so the test is not vacuous. SAME FUNCTIONS, NOT REIMPLEMENTATIONS: risk is pref/kl against pref/c-distribution, the same call efe.clj:659-668 makes; ambiguity is reached through #'efe/ambiguity (efe.clj:37-61), the private var efe.clj:679 itself calls -- the discipline C487 control 2 used; tau is policy/effective-temperature; ln E is habit-prior/log-priors; F_pi is policy-free-energy/f-pi-for-candidate; the posterior is policy/selection-scores and policy/softmax-weights; the choice is policy/select-action. NO RULING AND NO REGISTRY WRITE: :covers-key :none, aif-equations.edn and control-map-edges.edn are untouched (negative_controls reports shared registries untouched), and nothing is written to :choices or :decisions. Replay only -- no live run, no run lock taken, nothing under data/ written, persist-decision! never called. NOTED, NOT FIXED: pointer_check.bb's root list has no futon3c root, so this row's central file cannot be cited in file.clj:NN form here without a false 'file not found'; futon3c pointers above are written as '.clj L11-L20'. Same defect class C472/C473/AC7 named, one repo over; appending a root is a p4ng change and outside this acceptance. GATES: clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings on the one changed .clj; futon4/dev/check-parens.el OK; clojure -X:test :patterns [\\\"futon2\\\\..*-test$\\\"] 1070 tests / 6890 assertions, 0 failures / 0 errors, measured against a same-tree baseline WITHOUT this ns of 1055 / 6754, so the delta is exactly this row's 15 / 136; negative_controls.sh PASS (16 negative, 10 positive); pointer_check.bb 758 pointers in 3 files, 0 unresolved."
