/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/claude-15-repl-buffer-snapshot-2026-08-31.txt:2487:**The scope to hold, stated up front.** Not a "proof engine". One frame with a terminal certificate, reconstructed step by step as a cascade: per step, the applicable patterns (`find`) with receipts naming the clause matched; the up-closure via `@why`; the precedence that reproduces the recorded order; then the AIF layer — which steps were probes (taken to learn whether a route was open) and whether the epistemic term changes the chosen step anywhere. That's `nonDegenerate` in the proof domain, and it's the microcosm again one level up in expressiveness. The refusal rule applies here more than anywhere: if a proof-state Tension can't be typed so that these IF clauses are evaluable, the packet says so instead of grepping tension words — which is exactly what D1 said would happen on prose sections.
