 same-mission frontier by varying the coverage-saturation threshold, rejects every truncated candidate, deduplicates identical policies, and explicitly reports `:no-policy-choice` unless at least two complete cascades survive. The expanded suite is green (42 tests, 159 assertions). I’m doing one read-only real-constructor smoke check now, because the unit seam is mocked and the Python/Clojure boundary is the highest-risk part.\n\nThe real boundary smoke produced two distinct complete policies and correctly marked the menu selectable. I’ve also completed the pure dark ranking seam: it reuses the paper’s unscaled-prior algebra, reports both the engineering-score winner and habit-conditioned winner, and refuses singleton or unscored menus. Nothing is yet called by the scheduled runner or persisted. I’m running the broader WM/full-loop regressions before handing this slice back.\n\nThe real boundary smoke produced two distinct complete policies and correctly marked the menu selectable. I’ve also completed the pure dark ranking seam: it reuses the paper’s unscaled-prior algebra, reports both the engineering-score winner and habit-conditioned winner, and refuses singleton or unscored menus. Nothing is yet called by the scheduled runner or persisted. I’m running the broader WM/full-loop regressions before handing this slice back.\n\nThe WM compliance work is now underway, dark and reduction-safe. No scheduled behavior changed.\n\nImplemented:\n\n- A topology-sensitive cascade-level \\(E_{\\text{cascade}}(\\pi)\\) kernel in [cascade_prior.clj](/home/joe/code/futon2/src/futon2/aif/cascade_prior.clj:48).\n- A real same-mission cascade candidate frontier in [cascade_lane.clj](/home/joe/code/futon2/scripts/futon2/report/cascade_lane.clj:88). A live smoke test produced two distinct complete policies.\n- Pure shadow ranking through the existing unscaled-prior softmax seam in [cascade_prior.clj](/home/joe/code/futon2/src/futon2/aif/cascade_prior.clj:163).\n- A staged compliance co