hematics; only Phase 4 introduces WM records, and only Phase 8 can affect live WM behavior.\n\nThe regime is now separated into eight promotion phases plus one optional experiment. The key boundary is: Phase 1 proves the shared API; Phase 2 proves operational recall in mathematics; only Phase 4 introduces WM records, and only Phase 8 can affect live WM behavior.\n\nI’ve turned it into an explicit gated build-test regime in [M-shared-memory-control-build-test.md](/home/joe/code/futon3c/holes/missions/M-shared-memory-control-build-test.md:1).\n\nThe phases are:\n\n1. **Baseline and contract freeze — complete**\n   P0 memory writing, additive WM baseline, and dark mission-control kernel.\n\n2. **Shared retrieval seam — next**\n   Bounded `endpoint + optional type` lookup, common compact memory projection, domain isolation, and memory-use receipts.\n\n3. **Zaif recall vertical slice**\n   Pattern search → earlier memory → selection/use receipt → independently checked mathematics outcome.\n\n4. **Lifecycle and repeated mathematics trials**\n   Challenge, supersession, as-of queries, correction lag, failure injection, and bounded repeated trials.\n\n5. **Dark WM use of the same interface**\n   WM memories and p4ng endpoints through the identical query/projection/receipt contract. No scheduler effects.\n\n6. **Outer strategic cascades**\n   Control-pattern cascades retrieve memories and construct reason-bearing mission frontiers, preserving blockers and policy holes.\n\n7. **Outcome model and centrality ablation**\n   Compare the additive baseline against cascade/memory models on frozen held-out evidence. Centrality is retired only if ablation supports it.\n\n8. **Strategic policies and \\(E_S\\), shadow-only**\n   Stable strategic policy identities and separate habits, predictions, support, and explanations.\n\n9. **Operator-gated canary**\n   Advice-only → confirm-to-enact → tightly bounded reversible autonomy.\n\nThe embedding experiment is an optional Phase 6b and is explicitly off the critical path.\n\nEach phase now specifies:\n\n- Build artifacts.\n- Unit, integration, live, negative, and failure-injection tests.\n- Acceptance criteria.\n- Evidential limits.\n- Rollback behavior.\n- Required completion report.\n\nThe immediate Phase 1 packet is deliberately split into two reviewable changes:\n\n1. futon1b bounded `end + optional type` query and contract tests.\n2. Shared compact projection/use-receipt contract consumed by both futon3c and futon2 fixtures.\n\nI also linked the regime from the [P0 handoff](/home/joe/code/futon3c/holes/CODEX-HANDOFF-p0-memory-record.md:9), [typed-memory mission](/home/joe/code/futon3c/holes/missions/M-typed-memories.md:16), and [WM strategic mission](/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/missions/M-wm-strategic-mission-selection.md:175). Documentation checks are clean; no runtime behavior changed.\n\nI’ve turned it into an explicit gated build-test regime in [M-shared-memory-control-build-test.md](/home/joe/code/futon3c/holes/missions/M-shared-memory-control-build-test.md:1).\n\nThe phases are:\n\n1. **Baseline and contract freeze — complete**\n   P0 memory writing, additive WM baseline, and dark mission-control kernel.\n\n2. **Shared retrieval seam — next**\n   Bounded `endpoint + optional type` lookup, common compact memory projection, domain isolation, and memory-use receipts.\n\n3. **Zaif recall vertical slice**\n   Pattern search → earlier memory → selection/use receipt → independently checked mathematics outcome.\n\n4. **Lifecycle and repeated mathematics trials**\n   Challenge, supersession, as-of queries, correction lag, failure injection, and bounded repeated trials.\n\n5. **Dark WM use of the same interface**\n   WM memories and p4ng endpoints through the identical query/projection/receipt contract. No scheduler effects.\n\n6. **Outer strategic cascades**\n   Control-pattern cascades retrieve memories and construct reason-bearing mission frontiers, preserving blockers and policy holes.\n\n7. **Ou