urn 49\n\nREASONING (plaintext available in rollout)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAGENT MESSAGES\nThe restarted JVM is fast, but the smoke test exposed one correctness defect: the materialized projection was serving a startup-era snapshot, so it ranked the right pattern using a superseded memory and omitted its current correction. I’m fixing that readiness/catch-up invariant first; once the live smoke is both fast and lifecycle-correct, I’ll proceed into the dark-only Phase 4 path.\n\nThe restarted JVM is fast, but the smoke test exposed one correctness defect: the materialized projection was serving a startup-era snapshot, so it ranked the right pattern using a superseded memory and omitted its current correction. I’m fixing that readiness/catch-up invariant first; once the live smoke is both fast and lifecycle-correct, I’ll proceed into the dark-only Phase 4 path.\n\nThe defect is at the store boundary, not in Phase 3 ranking: Futon1b builds its current-memory index before XTDB has necessarily finished replaying. I’m adding an XTDB transaction-watermark invariant so an index is only published from a stable snapshot and any later catch-up drift forces a coherent rebuild. A regression test will write behind the projection and require the next read to self-heal.\n\nThe defect is at the store boundary, not in Phase 3 ranking: Futon1b builds its current-memory index before XTDB has necessarily finished replaying. I’m adding an XTDB transaction-watermark invariant so an index is only published from a stable snapshot and any later catch-up drift forces a coherent rebuild. A regression test will write behind the projection and require the next read to self-heal.\n\nThe regression is now green, along with Futon1b’s 39/39 and 59/59 suites; lint and structural checks are clean. 