endent reviewer/checker, responsible for outcome evidence and detecting provenance, explanation, budget, or tripwire failures.\n- Current additive controller: retained as the counterfactual baseline.\n- Phase 7 model: supplies advice only; it neither selects nor enacts.\n\nBefore the click, freeze:\n\n- admissible policies and blocked alternatives;\n- strategic recommendation and additive baseline;\n- `E_S`, predicted `G_S`, support relations, memories, budget, and tripwires;\n- Joe’s actual choice.\n\nAfterward, codex-6 should independently record useful progress or failure, memories materially used, overrides, prediction error, and rollback reason. Zai-8 must not certify its own outcome.\n\nFresh agents are especially valuable here: they test whether policy-conditioned memories and explanations survive session boundaries rather than succeeding through conversational carry-over. A new durée also gives the first genuine observation for the real advice window.\n\nI would not treat one successful click as permission for confirm-to-enact. It should be observation 1 in a reviewed advice-only series.\n\nTOOL DIGEST\n[none]"}, :session-id "019f8b63-a009-79e0-9a22-e7402848c822", :tags [:codex :turn-round :codex-rollout :codex-4], :at "2026-07-23T21:02:22.100Z", :type :coordination, :subject #:ref{:type :agent, :id "codex-4"}, :author "codex-4", :claim-type :step, :id "e-codexroll-019f8b63-t056"} #:evidence{:body {:session-uuid "019f8b63-a009-79e0-9a22-e7402848c822", :turn-id "019f90cb-062f-75c2-aecc-c239b980567a", :event-seq-range [4738 4767], :reasoning-encrypted-only-count 7, :tool-digest-count 8, :rollout-file "/home/joe/.codex/sessions/2026/07/22/rollout-2026-07-22T20-53-09-019f8b63-a009-79e0-9a22-e7402848c822.jsonl", :turn 57, :event :turn-round, :truncated? false, :message-count 4, :harvester-version 1, :reasoning-count 7, :profile :codex-rollout, :text "Codex rollout turn 57\n\nREASONING (plaintext available in rollout)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAGENT MESSAGES\nT