worklist.edn-203-   :review "Repair review at futon3c 44b714ed (which sits on top of 27a0f6d5) in an isolated sibling worktree (/home/joe/code/futon3c-review-loop, created at 44b714ed, removed afterwards, exit 0); the live JVM (:7070/:6768) was never touched and nothing was loaded into it. Gates re-run there with exit codes read directly, no pipe: clj-kondo --lint test/futon3c/agents/zai_memory_tool_contract_test.clj exit 0, 0 errors 0 warnings; futon4/dev/check-parens.sh on the same file exit 0 (OK); clojure -M:test -n futon3c.agents.zai-memory-tool-contract-test exit 0, 20 tests / 196 assertions, 0 failures 0 errors -- the row's numbers are exact (194 -> 196 is the repair swapping four assertions for six). THE PRIOR REVIEW FINDING IS FIXED, by repair route (a). The deftest at 178, now runner-records-r16-ask-and-yield-decision-witnesses, no longer re-derives an arm keyword from the stub's assistant text. It feeds two synthetic input maps in through :zaif-inputs-fn -- a real production option, not a test-only hook (src/futon3c/agents/zai_api.clj:1141-1145 reads it, :1333 destructures it, :1515 threads it, and zaif_inputs.clj:255 documents it) -- lets the runner reach zaif/dual-decide, and reads the persisted :zaif-arm-choice entries back out of the evidence store; that event name and its :constant-label are built in production at zaif_controller.clj:195-216, not in the test. Per turn it asserts exactly 2 witnesses, arm set = #{expected-arm}, constant-label set = #{:shipped :sweep}. I checked the arithmetic against the shipped constants rather than trusting the labels: for the :ask case retrieve = 0.1 - 0.0005*800 = -0.3, act = 1.0 * gamma 1.0 * 0.1 = 0.1, ask = 1.0 - 0.65 = 0.35 shipped and 1.0 - 0.15 = 0.85 sweep, yield = 0.0, so :ask wins under both constants; for the :yield case retrieve = 0.0 - 0.4 = -0.4 (idf-ish of nil observations is 0.0), act = -1.0, ask = -0.65 / -0.15, yield = 0.0, so :yield wins under both. I also falsified it rather than only reading it: changing the first expected arm from :ask to :act in the worktree copy made the run fail at line 208 with actual (not (= #{:act} #{:ask})), exit 1 -- so the assertion binds to what production computes, not to a literal (file restored, then the worktree removed). The other two deftests are unchanged since the first review pass and still hold: 156 drives all 28 registry tool names through the production round loop and asserts that set equals the names from (#'zai/openai-tools :full); 231 pins the tracked WM fixture, and I re-read all six asserted fields out of wm-contract/runs/U12-c-mis-falsifier/node-fixtures/801976e7-R16.edn myself -- :node :R16, :run/id 801976e7-01c6-4e39-aada-27f620f7c2f1, :via 'enactment', :basis 'S7: R16 enactment data does not exist until a flight flies', :status :absent, :reason :no-enactment-yet. git ls-files --error-unmatch succeeds on that fixture, so it is TRACKED and no SKIP guard is owed. Pointers land: the three new deftests begin at 156, 178 and 231 and the last ends at 245 (next deftest at 247), so the row's 156-245 range is right and the U10 222 -> 231 pointer fix was needed and correct. The U10 R16 :shared-machinery note no longer claims ask/yield ENDINGS; it now says the companion test drives the :zaif profile through production dual-decide and asserts the persisted :ask and :yield arm-choice witnesses for both constants, which is what the code does -- so :gap nil and :spec-test :covered are now true of all three clauses of the recorded gap (memory-family-only closed by 28/28 registered tools; ask/yield closed by the decision witnesses; the no-enactment datum honestly pinned as a typed absence). Commits are path-scoped and there is no --amend: futon3c 44b714ed touches one test file, 24 insertions / 15 deletions, parented on U11e c7bd2e24 with 27a0f6d5 an ancestor of it and both ancestors of master; futon2 4585cab touches two files, both under holes/labs/zaif-harness, and its worklist hunk is confined to this row. WORTH RECORDING, not blocking: the :ask inputs (operator-c-uncertainty 1.0 against act-value 0.1) sit deliberately outside the range that test/futon3c/agents/zaif_controller_test.clj:216 calibration-ask-arm-unreachable-at-shipped-cost calls typical, where it records that the shipped 0.65 keeps :ask from winning. The two are consistent (0.7 - 0.65 = 0.05 loses to a typical act-value; 1.0 - 0.65 = 0.35 beats 0.1), but the R16 :ask witness is produced by beliefs a live turn at the shipped constant would rarely present. MINOR, the same caveat U18z-U21z carry: workspace-root resolves to /home/joe/code and the fixture is slurped from the futon2 WORKING TREE, so the pin reads whatever revision futon2 is checked out at rather than 4585cab, and it throws rather than SKIPs if futon2 is absent. Nothing needed fixing by me this pass."}
