loses at 236 (next form 238), and the deftest ran 464-516 at that sha (516 was the file end). Commits are path-scoped with no --amend: futon3c 4dc5a9db touches only src/ and test/ zaif_controller, 119 insertions 0 deletions, parented on the U22z repair 44b714ed and an ancestor of master; futon2 b6038cb touches two files, both under holes/labs/zaif-harness, and its worklist hunk is confined to this row. The U10 R17 entry moves :spec-test :partial -> :covered, adds the line-464 pointer with :provenance :real and the record id, and clears :blocked-by [:S7] -- right, because this test draws on the tracked D9 report, not on S7 enactment material. FINDING, FIXED BY ME in one edit (futon3c 1b294a74, test file only): the report A/B half was unasserted. The pinned pair is non-divergent, so :divergent? could have been hardcoded false and the per-label :arm-counts mapping could have swapped :shipped and :sweep, and every assertion would still pass; the :incomplete branch was never reached at all. I extended the same deftest with a divergent pair built by production dual-decide + decision-evidence-entry over the c-uncertainty 0.5 inputs the file already pins at line 347 (shipped :act, sweep :ask) and with a half pair. It now asserts :arm-counts {:shipped {:act 1} :sweep {:ask 1}}, :divergent? true, divergent-pair-count 1, receipt-count 2, and :incomplete with replayed-pair-count 0 for the half pair. Falsified the same way: stubbing :divergent? to false failed lines 544 and 545, exit 1. Gates re-run after the fix in the same worktree: kondo 0/0 exit 0, parens OK exit 0, 24 tests / 112 assertions exit 0. The U10 pointer still reads line 464, the deftest start, so it needed no update. WORTH RECORDING, not blocking. (a) receipt-learning-summary has no production caller -- grep over src finds the defn and nothing else, the only call sites are in the test -- so the recorded gap clause about a shared learning path is closed as code, not as running wiring; the U10 note is honest about this, it now says WM BMR/A4A remains a separate learning path rather than claiming zaif reaches it. (b) The receipts are constructed in-test from the pin inputs by production decision-evidence-entry; nothing reads receipts back out of an evidence store into the summary, so recorded-not-live holds but store round-trip does not. (c) The pin itself is not new -- d9-live-replay-scores-select-the-arm at line 41 already pins the same record; what is new here is the pair replay. (d) The same caveat U18z-U23z carry: workspace-root resolves to /home/joe/code and the report is slurped from the futon2 WORKING TREE, so the test reads whatever revision futon2 sits at, and it throws rather than SKIPs if futon2 is absent."}
