worklist.edn:239:   :review "Reviewed 2026-09-03 (review seat; the design/build lane was claude-2 + codex-18 with claude-1 reviewing the design, so author != reviewer). (1) futon2 status clean except untracked build-loop.lock/.log; all 12 evidence shas read; every futon3c commit path-scoped to src/futon3c/agents/zaif_{actand,arm_adapters,arm_comparison}.clj plus its test file, every futon2 commit to the design doc or the artifact alone; author date == commit date on all 12, so no --amend. (2) GATES RE-RUN in an isolated sibling worktree at c7bd2e24 (futon3c-review-loop, removed after; no live JVM touched): the three namespaces gave 'Ran 20 tests containing 56 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors' with exit 0 captured directly; clj-kondo 0 errors 0 warnings; futon4/dev/check-parens.el OK. (3) HEADLINE RECOMPUTED from the tracked calibration file independently of the code: 114 sessions in four (actand, arm) groups -- (gamma,true)->:ask n=28 gold=18, density 9/14 and 5/14, act 0.2513144282809061; (nil,false)->:act n=77 gold=13, act -1.085708883832202; (c-channel,true)->:ask n=8 gold=0 and (actand,true)->:retrieve n=1 gold=0, both -Inf; 28+77+8+1=114. DISTINCT 3 against both named baselines at 1 -- the headline holds. The pinned demo value is ln(9/14)-ln(1/2) and equals 0.2513144282809061 exactly, matching the test assertion and the artifact. (4) ARTIFACT FRESHNESS ESTABLISHED rather than assumed: re-ran comparison-report over the tracked corpora in the review worktree and diffed against the committed runs/U11e-comparison-v1.edn -- IDENTICAL. (Worth noting for later: no test and no regenerate script tie the file to the runner, and the artifact carries no :replay-command, unlike D9's; I checked it by hand this time.) Rider numbers recomputed too: arm-A probe 0.14/0.56 from policy.clj:54-63, arm-B 0.8/0.2 from mission_head.clj:139, calibration plants ln(6/7)=-0.15415067982725827 and ln(12/7)=0.5389965007326869; digest comparisons 4*(114+39)=612, violations 0. (5) PINS OPENED: calibration pin e-0cae94f2-9ca8-4863-9251-44278445a5f7 is present with route :gamma, is_correction true, gold_judged true, and is one of the 28 record-ids the pinned row carries; R2 fixture 801976e7 carries :mission-health 0.023376623376623377 and :support-coverage 0.6, and :phase-progress is genuinely absent from its 14 :value channels. (6) The tests carry no SKIP guard and do not need one: calibration-sessions.edn is tracked, and node-fixtures is 40 tracked files = 39 EDN (the runner's 39) + README, with 3 -R2 fixtures (the adapters test's 3). (7) DEFAULT OFF verified by untruncated grep over *.clj/*.cljc/*.cljs/*.bb/*.edn in futon3c: nothing outside the three new files and their tests requires zaif-actand/-arm-adapters/-arm-comparison, so no production path reaches the source. -Inf also cannot reach the controller: actand-value (zaif_inputs.clj:69-72) accepts only a FINITE :act-value/:pragmatic-value/:expected-utility, so -Inf falls through task-belief-from (:79-91) to :d8/invalid-task-belief-source. (8) REGISTRY: :task-belief-actand-source landed in futon2 holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn at 726af003 with all three arm sites, :status :open and no comparison numbers imported; its text agrees with design section 3 up to the declared mechanical changes (glyph spelled out, indentation); signed cb6cc3aa. FINDING, FIXED BY THE REVIEWER IN THIS COMMIT: :acceptance and design section 6 name three corpora and the comparison replayed two -- the 56-decision bounded snapshot appears nowhere in the report or the artifact, with no reason recorded. Added [A5-addendum] to runs/U11-actand-design-v1.md giving (a) why a pure runner cannot reach it (the 56 decisions exist only behind D9's 127.0.0.1:7073 evidence query and section 6's last bullet forbids live JVM reads), (b) what its column would have held, provable from code without the query: hydrate-inputs returns exactly seven keys (zaif_inputs.clj:246-252), which is the shape of each persisted :inputs-snapshot, and none of arm A's seven source paths, none of arm B's four [:channels ...] paths and none of :route/:is_correction/:gold_judged is among them, so the column reads 56 typed :q-actand/missing-input refusals with 0 produced and 0 distinct and cannot move the headline either way, and (c) that the 39 node fixtures stand in for the mission grain, not for the 56 decisions. SECOND POINT, RECORDED NOT FIXED (same addendum): the [A2a] ordering probe and the floor plant are per ARM, not per (arm, corpus) -- the identical synthetic pair is reported inside both corpus cells of a column, so a cell can read :ordering-probe :pass in a corpus where the arm produced 0 values (arm A over the mission fixtures). Section 6 [A2a] asked for a per-corpus plant. The values are visibly planted and no headline number depends on them, so this is left standing as a declared limitation rather than reopening the row."
