worklist.edn:244:   :statement "Build the actand-indexed world-model source for :task-belief (prerequisite named by D8a's finding :d8/task-belief-actand-source-absent): Z1 promised initial gamma/C/actand tables with provenance (M-zaif-harness.md:187-194); gamma and C exist, the actand table was never built. JOINT PASS AGREED with claude-1 (bellback on invoke-1788372741639, 2026-09-02 ~18:20): claude-2 LEADS the design pass, claude-1 contributes wm-side constraints as review input. The design produces ONE grain-indexed statement in DESIGN-c-vector.md section-5 style (Q_actand : grain -> action -> Density over declared observables) so zaif's arm-grain source and the WM's mission-grain Q(o|pi) hole (DESIGN-c-vector.md section 3) are the same object at two indices -- building two incompatible forward models would recreate the two-C mistake one node over. THREE arms in the registry :choices entry: (A) futon3c portfolio/policy.clj:49-74; (B) futon3c aif/mission_head.clj:135-176; (C) the S6 cascade-catalog playout record (wm-side, NOT built -- named so the registry records it). Arms A/B are runnable over recorded data, so per Joe's 2026-09-01 rule the comparison run is designed into the row, not ruled on in advance. Provenance discipline: a predicted outcome with no typed source is a refusal (D8b's seam), never a prior. NOTE: distinct from wm-contract's own :U11 (C_mis build); same-name different boards."
