worklist.edn:272:   :statement "Eliminate direct-buffer dependency from invoke-jobs persist entirely (2026-09-03 morning finding: pool pinned at 4294693329/4294967296 by legacy live-thread buffer caches; even 1MB chunks cannot reserve from cold threads, so Drawbridge-side persists fail while warm HTTP threads succeed -- intermittent again until JVM restart). D13's 1MB chunking caps NEW caches but cannot free old holders. Wanted: persist via heap-backed IO (e.g. FileOutputStream/BufferedWriter or Channels/newChannel over a heap buffer) so ledger writes never touch the direct pool, preserving the existing tmp+force+atomic-rename structure and stage hook."
