holes/labs/zaif-harness/worklist.edn:189:   :review "Reviewed at futon3c 6784d6d4 in an isolated sibling worktree (/home/joe/code/futon3c-review-loop, created at that sha, removed afterwards, exit 0); the live JVM (:7070/:6768) was never touched and nothing was loaded into it. Gates re-run there with exit codes read directly, no pipe: clj-kondo --lint test/futon3c/agents/zaif_inputs_test.clj exit 0, 0 errors 0 warnings; bash futon4/dev/check-parens.sh on the same file exit 0 (OK); clojure -M:test -n futon3c.agents.zaif-inputs-test exit 0, 26 tests / 99 assertions, 0 failures 0 errors -- the row's numbers reproduce exactly. LIVE-PIN rule holds and BOTH data files are TRACKED (git ls-files --error-unmatch succeeds on M-zaif-harness/b1-gamma-mission.edn and wm-contract/runs/U12-c-mis-falsifier/node-fixtures/801976e7-R14.edn), so no SKIP guard is owed. I read every pinned number back out of the files myself: b1-gamma-mission.edn cell M-futon-forward-model carries :policy-precision 0.7071067811865476, :samples 10, :mean-perf -0.5 over a ten-long -0.5 perf-history, and evidence id e-63c25e11-ac8b-4287-966e-bdc7f007bc78 is present in :events (cell M-points-de-fuite, 2026-07-11T12:39:10Z); fixture 801976e7-R14.edn carries :node :R14, :run/id 801976e7-01c6-4e39-aada-27f620f7c2f1, :status :present, :via futon2.report.war-machine/invoke-strategic-selection, :field [:decision :tau], :value 1.0. The first deftest is a replay, not a data restatement: five -0.5 corrections folded through futon2.aif.selection-gain/update-selection-gain clear the min-history 5 burn-in and land on 2^(1.0 * -0.5) = 0.7071067811865476, the same value the record holds from ten samples of the same mean -- so the shipped transfer function reproduces the recorded policy-precision. The 0.2 in the last assertion is likewise production-derived, not magic: adaptive-temperature([0.0 1.0]) = spread/k = 1.0/5.0 with the default k 5.0, divided by gain 1.0. The monotonicity assertion (corrected gain 0.7071 raises tau above gain 1.0) runs futon2.aif.policy/effective-temperature both times. The second deftest is a pure data pin -- it reads the tracked R14 fixture and asserts its six fields, no production code -- which is weaker than the first, and is the same shape U20z WM half took. NOTED, not blocking: the typed-empty half of the first deftest is planted by construction. :status :absent / :reason :no-verdict-events exist nowhere in production (grep -rn no-verdict-events over futon2/src futon2/test futon3c/src futon3c/test, run untruncated, returns exactly two lines, both in the new test), so those two assertions restate a map literal defined three lines above and cannot fail. That is what the row own gap text asked for (no PLANTED verdict-stream direction/typed-empty test), so :gap nil is honest as written, but the direction half is what carries real coverage. Coverage pointers 106 and 136 land exactly on the two new deftest forms and the row 106-146 range ends on the last line of the second (next deftest is at 148). Commits are path-scoped (futon3c 6784d6d4: one test file, 44 insertions / 0 deletions; futon2 48d8a87: U10-node-coverage.edn + worklist.edn, and the worklist hunk touches only this row) and 6784d6d4 is an ancestor of futon3c master sitting directly on U20z 3607afa4 with no --amend. Unlike U20z, the coverage edit landed on the right node: R14 entry got the pointers and the :spec-test :partial -> :covered flip, R4/R8 untouched. TWO SMALL FIXES APPLIED BY ME to runs/U10-node-coverage.edn. (1) The line-106 pointer carried no :record-id, so the B1 record the test pins was unreachable from U10 -- the sibling pointers at R8 and at R14 line 136 all carry one; I added :record-id e-63c25e11-ac8b-4287-966e-bdc7f007bc78. (2) R14 :shared-machinery :note still claimed that the zaif tests only exercise gamma lookup/default, which the new test at line 106 falsifies -- it runs futon2.aif.selection-gain and futon2.aif.policy from the futon3c test file; I rewrote the note to say what that test actually computes and to record that the typed-empty half is planted, with the grep behind that claim. Minor, not blocking (the same caveat U18z, U19z and U20z carry): workspace-root resolves to /home/joe/code and harness-artifact slurps futon2 WORKING TREE, so these tests read whatever revision futon2 is checked out at rather than 48d8a87, and they throw rather than SKIP if futon2 is absent."
