holes/labs/zaif-harness/worklist.edn:261:   :review "Reviewed 2026-09-03 by the build-loop review seat (not the author: cb0d38fc is the work seat's D14 packet; my only authorship here is the review fix 67faf9f2 below). futon2 tree clean but for untracked runs/ receipts. Diff read in full (futon3c cb0d38fc, 2 files, 100+/22-). GATES REPRODUCED in isolated sibling worktree futon3c-review-d14 at cb0d38fc, exit codes captured directly via PIPESTATUS, never against the live JVM: clj-kondo 0 errors/0 warnings exit 0 (one pre-existing info at http.clj:7198, far from the diff); check-parens OK exit 0; futon3c.transport.invoke-ledger-atomicity-test 9 tests/38 assertions 0 failures exit 0 -- the claimed numbers exactly. TEST IS LOAD-BEARING (negative control): with the parent's http.clj (ae88efe7) restored and the new test kept, the same run gives 5 failures/9 tests -- the packet's test cannot pass without the packet's code. LIVE PIN VERIFIED against /tmp/futon3c-invoke-jobs.edn (read-only): job invoke-1787750995295-1507-0f434f39 exists and both values the new test quotes are verbatim -- :state \"failed\", :finished-at \"2026-08-26T13:29:56.668288653Z\". The test inlines these constants rather than reading the untracked file at run time, so no SKIP guard is owed. ENUMERATION CLAIM CHECKED, not trusted: the docstring's \"neither contains dangling job ids\" presumes :jobs/:job-order/:trace->job are the only job-id-bearing containers. Untruncated check -- bb read of the live ledger gives top-level keys exactly (:job-order :jobs :next-seq :trace->job :version), default-invoke-jobs-ledger (http.clj:317-323) agrees, and `grep -nE '(assoc|update|assoc-in|update-in) (ledger|l) :' src/futon3c/transport/http.clj` returns one line (556). So all three containers are pruned and there is no fourth. Separately confirmed :next-seq is `(inc (or (:next-seq ledger) 0))` (http.clj:727) and is never derived from (count jobs), so dropping records cannot rewind the counter or reuse a job id -- the failure mode that would have made this change unsafe. BEHAVIOUR CHECKED AGAINST LIVE DATA, not only the synthetic fixture: replaying the horizon over a snapshot of the real 7,613-job ledger drops 2,153 and keeps 5,460 (14.8MB -> ~10.9MB), and 0 terminal jobs have a missing or unparseable :finished-at, so the conservative never-drop branch has no live population hiding in it. No cross-namespace regression: the other 6 ledger-touching test namespaces give an IDENTICAL failure set at cb0d38fc and at its parent (84 tests/263 assertions, 31 failures/1 error both times, failing test names diffed and equal) -- those failures are pre-existing and untouched by D14. ONE FINDING, FIXED BY THE REVIEWER (futon3c 67faf9f2, path-scoped): the sentinel branch's closing assertion read :events-trimmed, but the aged-job fixture already sets :events-trimmed :d13/rolling-expiry, so it passed whether or not compaction ever touched the retained tombstone -- a vacuous assertion in the one place the corruption sentinel is proven. Replaced with :events, which the fixture lacks and only compact-terminal-job can add; NEGATIVE CONTROL run (compaction stage forced off): the new assertion fails with \"the retained sentinel is compacted, not passed through\", so it guards something real. Also commented why the D13 test's clock moved 2026-09-02 -> 2026-08-28 (it must stay inside the new 7-day horizon or that test silently starts asserting the wrong one) -- the diff moved it with no explanation. Post-fix in the same isolated worktree: 9 tests/39 assertions green, kondo 0/0, parens OK, all exit 0. THREE RESIDUALS, typed not papered, none blocking: (a) the horizon covers terminal states only, so the 98 live non-terminal jobs (93 \"delivered\", 4 \"deduped\", 1 \"running\") are retained by both horizons forever; the 93 delivered were all created 2026-08-27..08-30 with none since, which from one snapshot I can call legacy residue or a state that stopped advancing but cannot distinguish -- small now, but the same monotonic shape D14 set out to kill. (b) The protection set fails OPEN: parked_on/load-state (parked_on.clj:81-88) catches any read error and returns empty-state, so a corrupt or unreadable park store silently yields protected #{}. Under D13 that over-compacted a transcript; under D14 the same silent condition DELETES the job and its index entries, and ensure-invoke-jobs-ledger! persists the result immediately (http.clj:563-568). The blast radius of an existing fail-open grew from lossy to unrecoverable; the fix belongs in parked_on, not here. (c) Relief is real but modest and, as with D13, only lands at JVM restart -- per D13's :acceptance-reload the direct-buffer pool still blocks cold-thread persists (that is D15)."
