holes/labs/zaif-harness/worklist.edn-278-   :review "Reviewed 2026-09-03 by the build-loop review seat (NOT the author of either half: 623c2969 is claude-2's emergency fix, already independently read by claude-1; ca6884b5 is the work seat's). Diff read for both shas. Gates REPRODUCED in isolated sibling worktree futon3c-review-d13 at ca6884b5, exit codes captured directly, never against the live JVM: clj-kondo 0 errors/0 warnings (one pre-existing info at http.clj:7169, far from the diff), exit 0; check-parens OK, exit 0; futon3c.transport.invoke-ledger-atomicity-test 8 tests/29 assertions, 0 failures, exit 0 -- the claimed numbers exactly. LIVE PIN VERIFIED against /tmp/futon3c-invoke-jobs.edn (read-only file read): job invoke-1787750995295-1507-0f434f39 -- all four values the test calls verbatim match the live record (:state \"failed\", :created-at 2026-08-26T13:29:55.295079374Z, :finished-at 2026-08-26T13:29:56.668288653Z, :event-seq 5); the fixture's event bodies are synthetic bulk and are not claimed as verbatim. Retention logic checked by hand, not just by test: parked-on/snapshot :index holds STILL-AWAITED deps and ensure! is a pure lazy disk load with no resume side effects, so composing compaction into swap-vals! is idempotent under CAS retry and safe inside the writer lock; a terminal job with :finished-at nil is never compacted (conservative -- the zombie case from this very incident); re-compacting an already-compacted job is a fixpoint. ENUMERATION CHECKED rather than taken on trust: grep -n \"!invoke-jobs-ledger\" src/futon3c/transport/http.clj confirms every mutation site is the two update fns plus resets, so \"every atomic ledger update\" holds; the cited line ranges 327-385, 538-540, 564-587 all resolve correctly. I enumerated the 81 distinct top-level job keys in the live ledger against compact-terminal-job's whitelist and traced every dropped key that code reads: :bell-type and :ref are read only for the job being executed (non-terminal), :inbox-path only on the \"delivered\" state (non-terminal), so no reader breaks. ONE FINDING, FIXED BY THE REVIEWER (futon3c ae88efe7, path-scoped): invoke-job-public-view (http.clj:1698-1706) did not expose :events-trimmed, so GET /api/alpha/invoke/jobs/<id> on a compacted job returned :result nil with nothing to distinguish an expired transcript from a job that never produced a result -- the silent-degradation shape this board keeps typing (cf. D8 micro-finding (a)). Fix adds the key to the view plus an assertion; NEGATIVE CONTROL run: the assertion fails with nil against the unpatched view, so it guards something real. Post-fix in the same isolated worktree: 8 tests/30 assertions green, kondo 0/0, parens OK, all exit 0. TWO RESIDUALS, typed not papered, neither blocking: (a) OUTSTANDING ACCEPTANCE -- \"live JVM reload recorded\" is NOT met and cannot be met by this loop (the review seat is forbidden the live JVM and the work seat deferred it by row protocol); the lane owner still owes the acceptance reload from /home/joe/code/futon3c master, and until then the expiry is code-only, not relief; (b) the expiry bounds per-record DETAIL (<2000 chars per tombstone, asserted) but not record COUNT -- 7,594 jobs of tombstone is still ~15MB and grows monotonically, so the ledger is bounded in the sense the row asked for and unbounded in another. Also noted: compaction overwrites the manual pass's :d13/compaction-20260902 provenance marker with :d13/rolling-expiry (cosmetic), and the 623c2969 chunk test proves a 3MB ledger round-trips but not that the write was chunked (a single write would also pass) -- the chunking itself rests on claude-1's read of the loop."
