    :review "Reviewed at futon3c 4dc5a9db in an isolated sibling worktree (/home/joe/code/futon3c-review-loop, created at that sha, removed afterwards); the live JVM (:7070/:6768) was never touched and nothing was loaded into it. Gates re-run there with exit codes read directly, no pipe: clj-kondo --lint on both changed files exit 0, 0 errors 0 warnings; futon4/dev/check-parens.sh on both exit 0 (OK); clojure -M:test -n futon3c.agents.zaif-controller-test exit 0, 24 tests / 106 assertions, 0 failures 0 errors -- the row numbers are exact. LIVE PIN: git ls-files --error-unmatch succeeds on runs/D9-tie-order-count.edn, so it is TRACKED and no SKIP guard is owed; I read the pin out of it myself -- [:live :count] 56 and [:live :live-pin :id] e-0f2f9aec-6240-40e9-a25a-e45d9452076f, whose :decision map has exactly the six keys the test select-keys, so the equality at line 494 is byte-for-byte and not a subset. I recomputed its numbers rather than trusting them: idf-ish over total-docs 106 with ten dfs of 1 is 10*ln(107/2) / (10*ln 107) = 0.8516643332946383, minus retrieve-token-cost 0.0005 * 212 tokens = 0.7456643332946383, the recorded :retrieve exactly; ask = 0.3 - 0.65 = -0.35000000000000003 shipped and 0.3 - 0.15 = 0.15 sweep, act 0.0, yield 0.0, so :retrieve wins under BOTH constants -- which is why the recorded arm-counts are {:shipped {:retrieve 1} :sweep {:retrieve 1}} and divergent-pair-count 0. Two falsifications in the worktree, both restored afterwards: (1) perturbing the idf-ish normalizer (Math/log (inc total)) to (Math/log (+ 1.001 total)) made line 494 fail with 0.7456626299524189, exit 1, so the pin binds to production arithmetic rather than to a literal; (2) deleting the arm-equality clause from receipt-learning-summary replayable? made lines 505 and 507 fail (:replayed for :non-replayable, 1 for 0), so the corrupted-receipt refusal really rides the replay, not the label. Pointers land: receipt-learning-summary opens at src line 173 and closes at 236 (next form 238), and the deftest ran 464-516 at that sha (516 was the file end). Commits are path-scoped with no --amend: futon3c 4dc5a9db touches only src/ and test/ zaif_controller, 119 insertions 0 deletions, parented on the U22z repair 44b714ed and an ancestor of master; futon2 b6038cb touches two files, both under holes/labs/zaif-harness, and its worklist hunk is confined to this row. The U10 R17 entry moves :spec-test :partial -> :covered, adds the line-464 pointer with :provenance :real and the record id, and clears :blocked-by [:S7] -- right, because this test draws on the tracked D9 report, not on S7 enactment material. FINDING, FIXED BY ME in one edit (futon3c 1b294a74, test file only): the report A/B half was unasserted. The pinned pair is non-divergent, so :divergent? could have been hardcoded false and the per-label :arm-counts mapping could have swapped :shipped and :sweep, and every assertion would still pass; the :incomplete branch was never reached at all. I extended the same deftest with a divergent pair built by production dual-decide + decision-evidence-entry over the c-uncertainty 0.5 inputs the file already pins at line 347 (shipped :act, sweep :ask) and with a half pair. It now asserts :arm-counts {:shipped {:act 1} :sweep {:ask 1}}, :divergent? true, divergent-pair-count 1, receipt-count 2, and :incomplete with replayed-pair-count 0 for the half pair. Falsified the same way: stubbing :divergent? to false failed lines 544 and 545, exit 1. Gates re-run after the fix in the same worktree: kondo 0/0 exit 0, parens OK exit 0, 24 tests / 112 assertions exit 0. The U10 pointer still reads line 464, the deftest start, so it needed no update. WORTH RECORDING, not blocking. (a) receipt-learning-summary has no production caller -- grep over src finds the defn and nothing else, the only call sites are in the test -- so the recorded gap clause about a shared learning path is closed as code, not as running wiring; the U10 note is honest about this, it now says WM BMR/A4A remains a separate learning path rather than claiming zaif reaches it. (b) The receipts are constructed in-test from the pin inputs by production decision-evidence-entry; nothing reads receipts back out of an evidence store into the summary, so recorded-not-live holds but store round-trip does not. (c) The pin itself is not new -- d9-live-replay-scores-select-the-arm at line 41 already pins the same record; what is new here is the pair replay. (d) The same caveat U18z-U23z carry: workspace-root resolves to /home/joe/code and the report is slurped from the futon2 WORKING TREE, so the test reads whatever revision futon2 sits at, and it throws rather than SKIPs if futon2 is absent."}
