worklist.edn:153:   :review "Reviewed 2026-09-03 (review seat; work seat was the claude-2 lane, not me -- I read the diffs cold and reproduced every number below). Gates re-run at cb8c9d15 in an isolated sibling worktree /home/joe/code/futon3c-review-loop (never the live JVM; :7070/:6768 untouched, no reload), each exit code captured directly, worktree removed after: clojure -M:test -n futon3c.agents.zaif-inputs-test exit 0, \"Ran 20 tests containing 62 assertions. 0 failures, 0 errors\" -- exactly the claimed 20/62; clj-kondo --lint on the test file exit 0, \"errors: 0, warnings: 0\"; check-parens (futon4/dev/check-parens.el, arxana-check-parens-cli) exit 0, \"OK\". NON-VACUITY: I mutated two pins in the worktree (114.21190142192009 -> 114.0 and the gamma factor 0.7071067811865476 -> 1.0) and re-ran: exit 1, 2 failures, one in each new deftest, the fixture assertion reporting actual 114.21190142192009 -- so both tests really reach the recorded values rather than asserting their own inputs. LIVE PIN: zaif_inputs_test.clj:121-140 reads futon2 holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/U12-c-mis-falsifier/node-fixtures/0a18c4f7-R5.edn, which git ls-files confirms is TRACKED, and cites run id 0a18c4f7-758e-400a-8223-9c52edf07450 in a comment; the fixture file carries that same :run/id, :node :R5, :status :present, :via \"futon2.aif.efe/rank-actions\", top action :target \"M-zaif-harness-v1\", and the three pinned doubles verbatim. No SKIP guard is needed: both data files the test depends on (the fixture and the gamma table) are tracked, and the cross-repo sibling-path resolution copies zaif_inputs.clj:28-46, which production already does. The G-core = G-risk + G-ambiguity assertion is not a tautology: the same fixture record carries :habit-prior-bias -5.117993812416755 and :predictability-bonus 13.975 that do NOT enter G-core, so the identity is a real property of the recorded ranking. SECOND PIN CHECKED: the gamma 0.7071067811865476 asserted at :109-110 (and already pinned pre-commit at :46-62 and :86) is the real tracked B1 cell -- futon2 holes/labs/M-zaif-harness/b1-gamma-mission.edn:81-85 gives \"M-futon-forward-model\" {:policy-precision 0.7071067811865476, :samples 10}, one of the few of the 18 cells that is not the uniform 1.0, which is what makes the attributed-act < unattributed-act assertion bite. MATRIX: the R5 entry going :partial -> :covered with :gap nil :blocked-by [] follows the R2 precedent set by U16z line-for-line (zaif-side test + WM-fixture test carrying :record-id); dropping :S7 is right even though S7 itself is still :blocked, because the ranked-actions fixture R5 needed has landed (R1/R3 still need the mu-pre/mu-post extraction and still list it). COMMITS: cb8c9d15 touches one file, 853868e two, both under holes/labs/zaif-harness; author date == committer date on all three, so no --amend. No new all/none enumeration claim was made, so that rule does not bind. REVIEWER FIX (one edit): the entry introduced :provenance :real-table, and U16z had introduced :registry-derived, neither documented in the matrix's :provenance-note vocabulary (\"real\"/\"planted\") -- I extended that note to name both. NOTED, not fixed: the :evidence line credits futon2 853868e but the string itself was finalised in 4081610 (the LEDGER_SHA back-fill), the same self-reference U16z's review recorded."
