/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/zaif-harness/worklist.edn:232:   :review "Reviewed 2026-09-03 (review seat; work seat was codex, so author != reviewer). Checked, all reproduced at HEAD: (1) futon2 status clean except untracked build-loop.lock/.log; both shas path-scoped to the single new runs/ file, 154 + 5 insertions, no --amend. (2) Every arm pointer read verbatim -- policy.clj:49 is pragmatic-value with :work-on at :54-63, :review :64-68, :consolidate :69-74, remaining cases :75-89, expected-free-energy at :155 feeding :terms :pragmatic at :178; mission_head.clj defns land exactly at 135/146/157/168/184 as cited. (3) Arm-C pointers: zaif worklist:83-85 is the S6 row, wm-contract worklist:819/822 are U23/U24, futon4 mission-lifecycle-wm-alignment.md items 1/2/3 sit at :153-161/:162-166/:167-173. (4) Enumerations re-run from futon2: calibration count printed 114; the seven-key channel probe printed {:rows 114, :hits 0}; the tick-record find printed exactly the three originals (git ls-files = 0, i.e. untracked as stated); the fixture find printed 39 (git ls-files = 40 = 39 EDN + README). (5) Live pins opened and matched byte-for-byte: 0a18c4f7-R2 carries :mission-health 0.023376623376623377 and :support-coverage 0.6 and has 14 observations; 801976e7-S4 carries mission-id M-zaif-harness-v1, endpoint futon2-d/mission/zaif-harness-v1, witness-rule selection-decision; R1/R3 are 417-entry; R16 is :absent :no-enactment-yet; e-0cae94f2 is the first calibration row id. The 56-decision numbers are quoted accurately from D8a:41-72 and U8a:54-79. FINDING, fixed by the reviewer in one edit (f1545a9): the sentence \"none of the 114 calibration rows or 56 decision snapshots contains these five channels\" is a none-claim, but only the calibration half carried a search command -- the 56-decision half pointed at the inventory, whose recorded counts ({:decisions 56, :nonempty-task-belief 0, :posting-stats-populated 56}) test task-belief emptiness, not those five channel names. The claim is nonetheless true and provable statically, which is stronger than a query over a growing store: zai_api.clj:1169 passes the hydrator output as :inputs, zaif_controller.clj:205 stores it verbatim as :inputs-snapshot, and zaif_inputs.clj:246-252 returns a closed seven-key map whose :observations is {:posting-stats ...} alone. I wrote that basis into the map at :39-48 and restated the evidence line ranges it shifted. No live JVM was touched (:7070/:6768 untouched, no reload, no :7073 query -- the 56-decision numbers were read from the committed receipts rather than re-queried). No tests were added, so the live-record-pin and untracked-SKIP test rules do not bind; the discovery pins are real record ids as the acceptance asks. worklist_check passed after the edit."
