/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/zaif-harness/worklist.edn:242:   :statement "Rung 2 of the zero-support ladder (J-ruling, registry efdc401 :task-belief-actand-source :decided; design [A5], futon2 8f470e2 -- READ IT, the kin relation is declared there): constructive generalization in zaif_actand.clj. For a group whose density has zero support for the target outcome, pool sessions over the v1 kin relation (same arm + same correction-label), emit a q-actand-record marked :constructed with :derivation {:rule :v1-kin-pool :kin [<group keys>]} and provenance = the UNION of kin record-ids -- never passed off as observed (the record shape must still pass the shared q-actand-record validator; extend the schema minimally if :constructed/:derivation keys need admitting, in the same commit as the validator test update). The demo bridge consumes constructed densities identically. FIRST LIVE CORPUS: the nine -inf sessions (c-channel x :ask 0/8, actand x :retrieve 0/1). [A5] predicts c-channel pools with gamma x :ask -> 18/36 -> bridge 0.0, and actand x :retrieve has NO kin (rung 3's trigger) -- VERIFY these predictions in-test against the real file, do not assume them."
